#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014769"
msgid "I think if Va'ruun society is to move past Jinan's heirs, having an authoritative figure is helpful."
msgstr "바룬 사회가 지난의 후계자들을 넘어서려면 권위적인 인물이 있는 게 도움이 될 거라고 생각해."

#. PROMPT: What's your opinion of House Veth'aal?
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SarahMorgan: House Veth'aal is clearly the most qualified.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 01137380
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014768"
msgid "But it's a thin line between exercising authority and being authoritarian."
msgstr "하지만 권위를 행사하는 것과 권위주의적이 되는 것 사이에는 미묘한 차이가 있지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: They shouldn't rely on me to make a decision. I won't always be there to help. &&& SarahMorgan: You have a point. And yet they weren't asking you to run their government, only to nudge it in the right direction. &&& SarahMorgan: Regardless, you did your best to navigate rough seas, both practically and politically.|And with the immediate threat dealt with, one hopes that Dazra will look forward to a brighter future.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: As it should be.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 0113737D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014767"
msgid "I did what I could. The rest is up to them."
msgstr "난 내가 할 수 있는 일을 했어. 나머지는 그들에게 달렸지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. PROMPT: They wouldn't be so foolish. I chose House Veth'aal because the city needs order.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: They wouldn't be so foolish. I chose House Veth'aal because the city needs order.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMSamCoe
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SamCoe: I will say that I don't mind you left them without a leader.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 01132666
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014766"
msgid "I can't abide by that. Law and order is one thing, but martial law is another."
msgstr "나로서는 용납 못 해. 법과 질서는 한 가지지만, 계엄령은 차원이 다른 문제야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: They shouldn't rely on me to make a decision. I won't always be there to help. &&& SarahMorgan: You have a point. And yet they weren't asking you to run their government, only to nudge it in the right direction. &&& SarahMorgan: Regardless, you did your best to navigate rough seas, both practically and politically.|And with the immediate threat dealt with, one hopes that Dazra will look forward to a brighter future.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Hopefully they will learn from the mistakes of the past.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 0113737B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014765"
msgid "Until the next experiment goes wrong, anyway."
msgstr "어쨌든 다음 실험이 잘못될 때까지는 말이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. PROMPT: Until the next experiment goes wrong, anyway.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Until the next experiment goes wrong, anyway.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 0113737A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014764"
msgid "Hopefully they will learn from the mistakes of the past."
msgstr "그들이 과거의 실수로부터 배우기를 바라야지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. PROMPT: Until the next experiment goes wrong, anyway.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Concerned
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SarahMorgan: In any case, I would call this mission a resounding success. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 0113737A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014763"
msgid "And that requires teaching the next generation those hard lessons."
msgstr "그리고 그러려면 다음 세대에게 그 힘든 교훈을 가르쳐야 해."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: They shouldn't rely on me to make a decision. I won't always be there to help. &&& SarahMorgan: You have a point. And yet they weren't asking you to run their government, only to nudge it in the right direction. &&& SarahMorgan: Regardless, you did your best to navigate rough seas, both practically and politically.|And with the immediate threat dealt with, one hopes that Dazra will look forward to a brighter future.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I have faith they will. If nothing else, they've proven to be extremely resilient.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 01137379
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014762"
msgid "The threat may be gone, but only time will tell if they recover from this."
msgstr "위협은 사라졌을지 모르지만, 그들이 이것으로부터 회복할지는 시간이 지나야 알 수 있을 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. PROMPT: The threat may be gone, but only time will tell if they recover from this.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: The threat may be gone, but only time will tell if they recover from this.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SarahMorgan: In any case, I would call this mission a resounding success. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 01137378
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014761"
msgid "I have faith they will. If nothing else, they've proven to be extremely resilient."
msgstr "난 그들이 그럴 거라고 믿어. 적어도 그들은 엄청난 회복력을 보여줬으니까."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Thinking / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: They shouldn't rely on me to make a decision. I won't always be there to help.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: They shouldn't rely on me to make a decision. I won't always be there to help.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Thinking
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SarahMorgan: Regardless, you did your best to navigate rough seas, both practically and politically.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 01137373
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014760"
msgid "You have a point. And yet they weren't asking you to run their government, only to nudge it in the right direction."
msgstr "네 말이 맞아. 하지만 그들은 네가 그들의 정부를 운영해 달라고 요청한 게 아니라, 단지 올바른 방향으로 이끌어 달라고 한 거였잖아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Veth'aal is clearly the most qualified. &&& SarahMorgan: Interesting. I personally disagree, which means our criteria must be markedly different. |House Veth'aal voted in favor of the Serpent's Crusade. That alone gives me pause. &&& SarahMorgan: That being said, I do question your decision to leave them without a Speaker.|You were given a chance to steer their government in the right direction. |As it stands now, I worry they will suffer from infighting and turmoil.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: As a strategic move it plays, but we're not at war with House Va'ruun. There was no need to weaken them.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 01137372
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01475F"
msgid "That's precisely why I did it. To weaken House Va'ruun."
msgstr "그래서 내가 그렇게 한 거야. 바룬 가문을 약화시키려고."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: SarahMorgan: You have a point. And yet they weren't asking you to run their government, only to nudge it in the right direction.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 01137375
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01475E"
msgid "Regardless, you did your best to navigate rough seas, both practically and politically."
msgstr "어쨌든, 너는 실질적으로나 정치적으로나 거친 바다를 항해하기 위해 최선을 다했어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Friendly
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Friendly
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Agreed. Things may look tough now, but their self-reliance and ingenuity will help them pull through this.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 01137375
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01475D"
msgid "And with the immediate threat dealt with, one hopes that Dazra will look forward to a brighter future."
msgstr "그리고 당면한 위협이 해결되었으니, 다즈라가 더 밝은 미래를 기대하기를 바라야지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Veth'aal is clearly the most qualified. &&& SarahMorgan: Interesting. I personally disagree, which means our criteria must be markedly different. |House Veth'aal voted in favor of the Serpent's Crusade. That alone gives me pause. &&& SarahMorgan: That being said, I do question your decision to leave them without a Speaker.|You were given a chance to steer their government in the right direction. |As it stands now, I worry they will suffer from infighting and turmoil.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: You have a point. And yet they weren't asking you to run their government, only to nudge it in the right direction.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 01137374
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01475C"
msgid "They shouldn't rely on me to make a decision. I won't always be there to help."
msgstr "그들이 결정을 내리는 데 나한테 의존해서는 안 돼. 내가 항상 도울 수 있는 건 아니니까."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: SarahMorgan: Yes. I know I will not make the mistake of doubting House Va'ruun. Even after all this.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 01137377
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01475B"
msgid "In any case, I would call this mission a resounding success."
msgstr "어쨌든, 이번 임무는 대성공이라고 할 수 있겠어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 01137377
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01475A"
msgid "I feel we have a better understanding of House Va'ruun's culture and politics, and the galaxy is just a tiny bit less hostile as a result."
msgstr "우리가 바룬 가문의 문화와 정치에 대해 더 잘 이해하게 되었고, 그 결과 은하계가 아주 조금 덜 적대적이 되었으니까."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: The city is doomed either way. I am not going to be the scapegoat when it does.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: The city is doomed either way. I am not going to be the scapegoat when it does.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Serious
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 0113736F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014759"
msgid "Interesting. I can picture a scenario where things go wrong, and you're blamed."
msgstr "흥미롭네. 상황이 잘못되고 네가 비난받는 시나리오를 상상할 수 있어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: The city is doomed either way. I am not going to be the scapegoat when it does.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SarahMorgan: Regardless, you did your best to navigate rough seas, both practically and politically.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 0113736F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014758"
msgid "But had you made a choice, perhaps that outcome could've been avoided. If nothing else, the new Speaker would be indebted to you."
msgstr "하지만 네가 선택을 했다면, 아마 그런 결과를 피할 수 있었을 거야. 적어도 새 대변자는 네게 빚을 졌을 테니까."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: SarahMorgan: Be that as it may, you were still began your journey as an outsider.|To go from a virtual stranger to their most trusted confidant in such a short time was no small feat.
#. ALIAS: SarahMorgan
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCFSarahMorgan
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SarahMorgan: Tell me... what influenced your decision to advocate for House Ka'dic?
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SarahMorgan
#. TOPIC: 01137376
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SarahMorgan_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014757"
msgid "I would like to pick your brain, however, regarding your choice of Speaker. Call it... intellectual curiosity."
msgstr "하지만 대변자를 선택한 것에 대해서는 네 생각을 좀 듣고 싶어. 말하자면... 지적 호기심이랄까."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Veth'aal is clearly the most qualified. &&& SarahMorgan: Interesting. I personally disagree, which means our criteria must be markedly different. |House Veth'aal voted in favor of the Serpent's Crusade. That alone gives me pause. &&& SarahMorgan: That being said, I do question your decision to leave them without a Speaker.|You were given a chance to steer their government in the right direction. |As it stands now, I worry they will suffer from infighting and turmoil.
