#. TOPIC: 01132674
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014536"
msgid "I don't know if that's true, but if that's your read, I hope it's right. In fact, the \"abstain\" vote might've been just a tactic."
msgstr "그게 사실인지는 모르겠지만, 네 분석이 그렇다면, 맞기를 바라. 사실, ‘기권’ 투표는 그저 전술이었을지도 몰라."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What are your thoughts on House Dul'kehf's leadership style? &&& SamCoe: I'm not going to say they're the best choice. Being from the Freestar Collective, I've had my fill of bureaucracy.|But if they're the only ones who aren't beating the war drum, they're okay in my book.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: They're spies, right? Can't trust a word they say. But sometimes you can guess what they're thinking, if you pay attention to the subtext.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 0113266F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014534"
msgid "What are your thoughts on House Ka'dic's leadership style?"
msgstr "카딕 가문의 통치 방식에 대해 어떻게 생각해?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. PROMPT: House Veth'aal will respect the decision of the council.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Veth'aal will respect the decision of the council.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMSamCoe
#. FACE: Concerned
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SamCoe: I will say that I don't mind you left them without a leader.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 0113266C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014533"
msgid "You got a lot more faith in them than I do. Now that Viktor is Speaker, the man has no reason to."
msgstr "나보다 그자들을 훨씬 더 신뢰하는군. 이제 빅토르가 대변자가 되었으니, 그럴 이유가 없는데도 말이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Ka'dic abstained from the vote for political reasons. &&& SamCoe: Yeah, maybe. It's always tough to be the deciding vote. The way they did it was sneaky as hell. &&& SamCoe: My guess? They probably KNEW how you were voting, and figured they would make YOU the bad guy.|Had they just voted their conscience, that'd mean House Veth'aal would be pissed at them. As it stands, their hands are clean.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: And that's exactly what I'm afraid of.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 0113266B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014531"
msgid "Viktor is in charge. Whatever he chooses, it's his call."
msgstr "빅토르가 책임자야. 그자가 뭘 선택하든, 그자 마음이지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. PROMPT: Viktor is in charge. Whatever he chooses, it's his call.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Viktor is in charge. Whatever he chooses, it's his call.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMSamCoe
#. FACE: Concerned
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SamCoe: I will say that I don't mind you left them without a leader.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 0113266A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014530"
msgid "And that's exactly what I'm afraid of."
msgstr "그리고 그게 바로 내가 두려워하는 점이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Ka'dic abstained from the vote for political reasons. &&& SamCoe: Yeah, maybe. It's always tough to be the deciding vote. The way they did it was sneaky as hell. &&& SamCoe: My guess? They probably KNEW how you were voting, and figured they would make YOU the bad guy.|Had they just voted their conscience, that'd mean House Veth'aal would be pissed at them. As it stands, their hands are clean.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I can't abide by that. Law and order is one thing, but martial law is another.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 01132667
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01452F"
msgid "They wouldn't be so foolish. I chose House Veth'aal because the city needs order."
msgstr "그렇게 어리석지는 않을 거야. 내가 베타알 가문을 선택한 건 도시에 질서가 필요하기 때문이야."

#. PROMPT: I expect them to initiate the Crusade as soon as they're ready.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I expect them to initiate the Crusade as soon as they're ready.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMSamCoe
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SamCoe: I will say that I don't mind you left them without a leader.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 01132668
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01452E"
msgid "So you chose them knowing that might happen? I hope you're joking."
msgstr "그런 일이 일어날 수 있다는 걸 알고도 그자들을 선택했다고? 농담이었으면 좋겠어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Apologetic
#. PROMPT: What do you think about House Veth'aal?
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What do you think about House Veth'aal?
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMSamCoe
#. FACE: Apologetic
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SamCoe: House Veth'aal will respect the decision of the council.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 01132664
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01452D"
msgid "I think they're bloodthirsty and militant. I admit, I don't know their whole story, but it's just the vibe I get."
msgstr "그자들은 피에 굶주렸고 호전적이라고 생각해. 그자들의 모든 내막을 아는 건 아니지만, 그냥 그런 느낌이 들어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Smirk
#. PROMPT: History is full of crusades, not just the Serpent's one.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: History is full of crusades, not just the Serpent's one.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMSamCoe
#. FACE: Smirk
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SamCoe: Either way, I'm not gonna worry about it too much.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 01132662
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01452C"
msgid "You would know better than I, professor. Glad the kid's got you to teach her."
msgstr "네가 나보다는 잘 알겠지, 교수 양반. 코라에게 너 같은 스승이 있다니 다행이군."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. PROMPT: They wouldn't be so foolish. I chose House Veth'aal because the city needs order.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: They wouldn't be so foolish. I chose House Veth'aal because the city needs order.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMSamCoe
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SamCoe: I will say that I don't mind you left them without a leader.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 01132666
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01452B"
msgid "I can't abide by that. Law and order is one thing, but martial law is another."
msgstr "난 그걸 용납할 수 없어. 법과 질서도 중요하지만, 계엄령은 또 다른 문제야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What do you think about House Ka'dic? &&& Barrett: I hate to punt the ball here, but I'm just a tourist. I don't know enough about Va'ruun culture or politics to form an educated opinion.|And scientifically speaking, I wouldn't want to make a decision like this without a full set of data.|But gastronomically speaking, I am glad you didn't go with House Veth'aal.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I don't know them, but I do know history. And historically militant governments are a pain in the you know what.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113232E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01452A"
msgid "What do you think about House Veth'aal?"
msgstr "베타알 가문에 대해 어떻게 생각해?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Agreed. They should've decided themselves. &&& SamCoe: Agree, one hundred percent. If they can't decide this now, what happens when you leave? Might as well make YOU the Speaker. &&& SamCoe: But at the end of the day, what's done is done. I know I'm burying the lede here, because you did save a whole city from ruin.|You gave them a starting point to rebuild and make a new future. |And thanks to you, the only "Crusade" Cora's gonna read about is in the history books.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Ha, very funny. If she can't, I have no idea what she's doing with those books.
