#. TOPIC: 0113265F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014529"
msgid "Cora can read? That's news to me."
msgstr "코라가 글을 읽을 수 있다고? 그건 또 처음 듣는 소리인데."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. PROMPT: I'm not closing the door on the Crusade happening.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I'm not closing the door on the Crusade happening.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMSamCoe
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SamCoe: Either way, I'm not gonna worry about it too much.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 01132660
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014528"
msgid "Well, you need to. Close it, lock it, throw away the key. Or else we'll have problems."
msgstr "음, 꼭 닫아둬야 해. 잠그고, 열쇠는 버려. 안 그러면 문제가 생길 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Agreed. They should've decided themselves. &&& SamCoe: Agree, one hundred percent. If they can't decide this now, what happens when you leave? Might as well make YOU the Speaker. &&& SamCoe: But at the end of the day, what's done is done. I know I'm burying the lede here, because you did save a whole city from ruin.|You gave them a starting point to rebuild and make a new future. |And thanks to you, the only "Crusade" Cora's gonna read about is in the history books.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: You and me both. But something like this doesn't go away in a year.
