msgid "Cora's probably read all that already."
msgstr "코라는 아마 그 책들을 이미 다 읽었을 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: SamCoe: Agree, one hundred percent. If they can't decide this now, what happens when you leave? Might as well make YOU the Speaker.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMSamCoe
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 01132657
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01451F"
msgid "But at the end of the day, what's done is done. I know I'm burying the lede here, because you did save a whole city from ruin."
msgstr "하지만 결국, 이미 벌어진 일은 벌어진 일이야. 나도 이게 핵심이 아니란 건 알아. 네가 도시 전체를 파멸에서 구했으니까."

#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMSamCoe
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: History is full of crusades, not just the Serpent's one.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 01132657
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01451E"
msgid "And thanks to you, the only \"Crusade\" Cora's gonna read about is in the history books."
msgstr "그리고 네 덕분에, 코라가 읽을 '뱀의 성전’은 역사책에나 나올 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Veth'aal will respect the decision of the council. &&& SamCoe: You got a lot more faith in them than I do. Now that Viktor is Speaker, the man has no reason to. &&& SamCoe: I will say that I don't mind you left them without a leader.|It's up to them to make a decision. Hell, do it the old fashioned way, have the people vote.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Agree, one hundred percent. If they can't decide this now, what happens when you leave? Might as well make YOU the Speaker.
