#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMSamCoe
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SamCoe: But at the end of the day, what's done is done. I know I'm burying the lede here, because you did save a whole city from ruin.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
#. TOPIC: 0113264F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_SamCoe_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014517"
msgid "As soon as you give the people a voice, the more you cut into that power structure."
msgstr "사람들에게 목소리를 줄수록, 그 권력 구조는 더 많이 약화할 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Veth'aal will respect the decision of the council. &&& SamCoe: You got a lot more faith in them than I do. Now that Viktor is Speaker, the man has no reason to. &&& SamCoe: I will say that I don't mind you left them without a leader.|It's up to them to make a decision. Hell, do it the old fashioned way, have the people vote.
#. ALIAS: SamCoe
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: If they were thinking that, joke's on them.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_SamCoe
