#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: They are. Real explorers have a responsibility not to cause harm. We're not colonizers, we're not agitators, we're here to observe and discover.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132359
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0144A0"
msgid "Exploration and destruction aren't mutually exclusive."
msgstr "탐험과 파괴가 서로 배타적인 건 아니잖아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Barrett is saying goodbye to the player for the last time, possibly. He valued time with the player but it's time to move on. / Confident
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: At the next port we'll go our separate ways.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132358
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01449F"
msgid "I hope in time you realize the scale of what you've done. The lives that you put in harm's way. But either way, I can't be a part of it."
msgstr "네가 한 일의 심각성을 언젠가 깨달았으면 좋겠어. 네가 위험에 빠뜨린 생명들 말이야. 어느 쪽이든, 난 거기에 가담할 수 없어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry
#. PROMPT: Exploration and destruction aren't mutually exclusive.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Exploration and destruction aren't mutually exclusive.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Angry
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: At the end of the day, you made a choice to start this "Serpent's Crusade."
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113235F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01449E"
msgid "They are. Real explorers have a responsibility not to cause harm. We're not colonizers, we're not agitators, we're here to observe and discover."
msgstr "그래. 진정한 탐험가들은 해를 끼치지 않을 책임이 있어. 우린 식민지 개척자가 아니야, 선동가도 아니야, 우린 관찰하고 발견하기 위해 여기 있는 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry
#. PROMPT: It is the will of the Great Serpent.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: It is the will of the Great Serpent.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Angry
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132354
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01449D"
msgid "Yeah, yeah, so I hear. The big snake in the sky, rubber stamping tens of thousands of deaths."
msgstr "그래, 그래, 나도 들었어. 하늘에 있는 커다란 뱀이 수만 명의 죽음에 도장을 찍었다고."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: VeryAngry
#. PROMPT: It is the will of the Great Serpent.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: VeryAngry
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132354
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01449C"
msgid "Well, this isn't the first time people have committed heinous acts in the name of some divine edict."
msgstr "글쎄, 신의 명령이라는 이름으로 끔찍한 짓을 저지른 건 이번이 처음이 아니지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: if this is hard to say feel free to change to "awful jerk" or something like that. / Angry
#. PROMPT: It is the will of the Great Serpent.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Angry
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: And the fact you did all this without considering how the rest of us would feel...
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132354
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01449B"
msgid "And it always turns out be some megalomaniac, doing megalomaniac things. Guess what that makes you."
msgstr "그리고 그건 항상 과대망상증 환자가 과대망상적인 짓을 하는 걸로 밝혀지지. 그게 널 뭘로 만드는지 알겠어?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: It is the will of the Great Serpent. &&& Barrett: Yeah, yeah, so I hear. The big snake in the sky, rubber stamping tens of thousands of deaths.|Well, this isn't the first time people have committed heinous acts in the name of some divine edict.|And it always turns out be some megalomaniac, doing megalomaniac things. Guess what that makes you. &&& Barrett: And the fact you did all this without considering how the rest of us would feel...|Constellation is about exploring the unknown, and keeping your mind and heart open to new discoveries.|Acts of aggression like this goes against who we are as a people.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: But it DOES matter. You made these decisions. You have to own them, justify them! 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132353
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01449A"
msgid "It doesn't matter. The decision has been made."
msgstr "상관없어. 결정은 이미 내려졌으니까."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: At the end of the day, you made a choice to start this "Serpent's Crusade."
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Angry
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: [Second Chance] I didn't realize the consequences of that choice. I'll try to make better decisions from now on. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132352
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014499"
msgid "I want you to open your eyes and see the consequences of that choice. And if you can't, then I can't be a part of it."
msgstr "네가 그 선택의 결과를 직시했으면 좋겠어. 그리고 그럴 수 없다면, 난 거기에 가담할 수 없어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry
#. PROMPT: It is the best thing for the Settled Systems.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: It is the best thing for the Settled Systems.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Angry
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: And the fact you did all this without considering how the rest of us would feel...
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132351
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014498"
msgid "What? In what universe is any of that true?"
msgstr "뭐? 도대체 어느 우주에서 그게 사실이야?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Shocked that the player is not apologizing. / Angry
#. PROMPT: Let's just agree to disagree.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Let's just agree to disagree.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Angry
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132350
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014497"
msgid "Are you kidding me? That's a cop out."
msgstr "장난해? 그건 비겁한 변명이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry
#. PROMPT: Let's just agree to disagree.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Angry
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: At the end of the day, you made a choice to start this "Serpent's Crusade."
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132350
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014496"
msgid "This isn't some political argument with no answer. This is the difference between right and wrong, life and death."
msgstr "이건 답이 없는 정치적 논쟁이 아니야. 이건 옳고 그름, 삶과 죽음의 문제라고."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I actually chose House Dul'kehf knowing it was the worst thing for Dazra. &&& Barrett: That's pretty messed up, but hey, it's on them for having you make that choice.|But I do know you make a damn persuasive argument.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: That's pretty messed up, but hey, it's on them for having you make that choice.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014495"
msgid "I actually chose House Ka'dic knowing it was the worst thing for Dazra."
msgstr "난 사실 다즈라에 최악의 선택이라는 걸 알면서도 카딕 가문을 선택했어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry
#. PROMPT: I did it knowing it would weaken Dazra.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I did it knowing it would weaken Dazra.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Angry
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014494"
msgid "And what about all the lives that will be lost in the process, on both sides? Did that ever enter your thought process?"
msgstr "그리고 그 과정에서 희생될 양측의 수많은 생명들은? 그런 건 생각해 본 적 있어?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant
#. PROMPT: I did it knowing it would weaken Dazra.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: And the fact you did all this without considering how the rest of us would feel...
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014493"
msgid "Of course it didn't. Sometimes I wonder if you even SEE things on that happen on the smaller scale."
msgstr "물론 없었겠지. 가끔은 네가 그 작은 규모의 일들을 보기나 하는지 궁금해."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Barrett loves the player. He says a warning to the player if they mess up again. / Concerned
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: We've been through so much, and are on this journey together.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Concerned
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014492"
msgid "But while I love you, that love is not unconditional."
msgstr "하지만 널 사랑하지만, 그 사랑은 무조건적인 게 아니야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Somber
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Somber
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014491"
msgid "The cavalier way you put lives in danger... it's murder. And that is a line that can't be crossed."
msgstr "네가 생명을 위험에 빠뜨리는 그 경솔한 방식... 그건 살인이야. 그리고 그건 넘지 말아야 할 선이야."

#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: *sigh*  I love you, but there are some things I can't forgive.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014490"
msgid "I'm going to stick with you for now, but please -- learn from this."
msgstr "당분간은 너와 함께 하겠지만, 제발 이번 일에서 교훈을 얻었으면 좋겠어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: A warning to the player. / Concerned
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: We've been through so much, and are on this journey together.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Concerned
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01448F"
msgid "Look, I'm willing to forgive you, but only if you're willing to learn and grown from this."
msgstr "봐, 난 널 용서할 의향이 있어. 하지만 네가 이걸 통해 배우고 성장할 의향이 있어야만 해."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Somber
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Somber
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: *sigh*  I love you, but there are some things I can't forgive.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01448E"
msgid "But please, take some time to think about your actions before you make them. Call me crazy, but I believe you can change."
msgstr "하지만 행동하기 전에 네 행동에 대해 잠시 생각해 봐. 내가 미쳤다고 할지 모르지만, 난 네가 변할 수 있다고 믿어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. PROMPT: House Veth'aal will bring much needed order and structure to Dazra.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Veth'aal will bring much needed order and structure to Dazra.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Concerned
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01448D"
msgid "Does the structure you're talking about include a barred door and no key?"
msgstr "네가 말하는 구조물에 잠긴 문과 열쇠가 없는 것도 포함이야?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. PROMPT: House Veth'aal will bring much needed order and structure to Dazra.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Concerned
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: But it did surprise me when you told them no one was fit to lead.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01448C"
msgid "Because that's what House Veth'aal likes to do."
msgstr "왜냐하면 그게 바로 베타알 가문이 하는 짓이거든."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: A parade would be fun. &&& Barrett: That's right! They could carry you around on a palanquin, and walk you through the city. And of course there'd be confetti. &&& Barrett: I also want to thank you for putting a halt to the Serpent's Crusade. |The last thing the Settled Systems needs is another war.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Well, I doubt House Va'ruun would've had the resources to invade the Settled Systems.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01448B"
msgid "What would've happened had we listened to Anasko?"
msgstr "우리가 아나스코의 말을 들었다면 어떻게 됐을까?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant
#. PROMPT: It won't be a full scale war.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: It won't be a full scale war.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Defiant
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01448A"
msgid "Maybe not at the start. But they're militant, focused, and fiercely determined."
msgstr "처음에는 아닐지 몰라도. 그들은 호전적이고, 집중력이 강하고, 결의에 차 있어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant
#. PROMPT: It won't be a full scale war.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: And the fact you did all this without considering how the rest of us would feel...
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113234A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014489"
msgid "Put that all together and you can do a lot of damage."
msgstr "그걸 다 합치면 엄청난 피해를 입힐 수 있지."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Let's just agree to disagree. &&& Barrett: Are you kidding me? That's a cop out. |This isn't some political argument with no answer. This is the difference between right and wrong, life and death. &&& Barrett: At the end of the day, you made a choice to start this "Serpent's Crusade." &&& Barrett: I want you to open your eyes and see the consequences of that choice. And if you can't, then I can't be a part of it.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Okay. I'll listen to what you have to say... but I'm not going to accept excuses.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132348
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014488"
msgid "Please hear me out, Barrett. I can explain."
msgstr "내 말 좀 들어봐, 배럿. 설명할 수 있어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: A parade would be fun. &&& Barrett: That's right! They could carry you around on a palanquin, and walk you through the city. And of course there'd be confetti. &&& Barrett: I also want to thank you for putting a halt to the Serpent's Crusade. |The last thing the Settled Systems needs is another war.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I don't know about that, dusty. On a scale of "picking a dessert" to "solving quantum gravity," this was definitely a piece of cake.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132344
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014487"
msgid "It was a tough choice."
msgstr "힘든 선택이었어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Thinking
#. PROMPT: What would've happened had we listened to Anasko?
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What would've happened had we listened to Anasko?
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Thinking
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132341
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014486"
msgid "Well, I doubt House Va'ruun would've had the resources to invade the Settled Systems."
msgstr "글쎄, 바룬 가문이 개척 성계를 침략할 자원이 있었을 것 같지는 않아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Amused
#. PROMPT: What would've happened had we listened to Anasko?
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Amused
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132341
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014485"
msgid "So it'd would've likely been guerilla tactics to start. Ambushes, sabotage, that kind of stuff."
msgstr "그래서 처음에는 게릴라 전술을 썼을 거야. 매복, 방해 공작, 뭐 그런 것들."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Worried
#. PROMPT: What would've happened had we listened to Anasko?
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Worried
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: The Crusade was Anasko's ambition. It was never the Serpent's will.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132341
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014484"
msgid "Then again, when has House Va'ruun ever fought in that manner? So I don't know. Let's just be glad we don't have to imagine it."
msgstr "그런데, 바룬 가문이 그런 식으로 싸운 적이 있었나? 그래서 나도 잘 모르겠어. 그런 상상을 하지 않아도 돼서 다행이라고 생각하자."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: 잠깐만. 먼저 이 말부터 꼭 해야겠어. |요즘 넌 어떻게 된 거야? 그동안의 네 행동은... 그냥 잘못됐어. 천문학적으로, 우주적으로, 잘못됐다고.|난 아직 널 버릴 생각은 없어, 두더지. 내가 순진한 건지 모르겠지만, 그래도 여전히 네 가슴 속 어딘가에 마음이 있다고 믿어. 그걸 증명하겠다고 엑스레이를 찍는 일은 없도록 하자고. &&& Barrett: 
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Yeah, yeah, so I hear. The big snake in the sky, rubber stamping tens of thousands of deaths.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132345
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014483"
msgid "It is the will of the Great Serpent."
msgstr "그것은 위대한 뱀의 뜻이다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Apologetic
#. PROMPT: What do you think about House Veth'aal?
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What do you think about House Veth'aal?
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Apologetic
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: House Veth'aal will bring much needed order and structure to Dazra.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132349
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014482"
msgid "I don't know them, but I do know history. And historically militant governments are a pain in the you know what."
msgstr "그들을 모르지만, 역사는 잘 알지. 그리고 역사적으로 호전적인 정부는 골칫거리거든."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: 잠깐만. 먼저 이 말부터 꼭 해야겠어. |요즘 넌 어떻게 된 거야? 그동안의 네 행동은... 그냥 잘못됐어. 천문학적으로, 우주적으로, 잘못됐다고.|난 아직 널 버릴 생각은 없어, 두더지. 내가 순진한 건지 모르겠지만, 그래도 여전히 네 가슴 속 어딘가에 마음이 있다고 믿어. 그걸 증명하겠다고 엑스레이를 찍는 일은 없도록 하자고. &&& Barrett: 
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: What? In what universe is any of that true?
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132343
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014481"
msgid "It is the best thing for the Settled Systems."
msgstr "그것이 개척 성계를 위한 최선의 선택이야."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: That's the problem with omnipotent beings. Poor communication skills.|Would make things a whole lot clearer if they just stopped by and talked to you.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: The whims of a cosmic snake aside, House Ka'dic seems like they'd be more open to peace.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132342
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014480"
msgid "Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed."
msgstr "어느 쪽이든, 다즈라의 새로운 지도부가 분별력이 있기를 바라."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I think Hasmak will be a good leader. &&& Barrett: From what I understand, he's a taskmaster.|Not my cup of tea. Rules and regulations are bad words in my dictionary.|But far large scale projects, it's usually for the best.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: As head of House Ka'dic, she's the spymaster, right? I've got a natural distrust of sneaky folks, built from watching years of low budget spy movies.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113233E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01447F"
msgid "I think Razma will be a good leader."
msgstr "라즈마가 훌륭한 지도자가 될 것 같아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Actually pissed off. / Angry
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: 잠깐만. 먼저 이 말부터 꼭 해야겠어. |요즘 넌 어떻게 된 거야? 그동안의 네 행동은... 그냥 잘못됐어. 천문학적으로, 우주적으로, 잘못됐다고.|난 아직 널 버릴 생각은 없어, 두더지. 내가 순진한 건지 모르겠지만, 그래도 여전히 네 가슴 속 어딘가에 마음이 있다고 믿어. 그걸 증명하겠다고 엑스레이를 찍는 일은 없도록 하자고.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Angry
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132340
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. INFO GROUP: COM_Barrett_AngerScene_Greet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01447E"
msgid "Okay, we need to talk about the Serpent's Crusade, because seriously, what the hell."
msgstr "좋아, 뱀의 성전에 대해 이야기 좀 해야겠어. 진지하게, 도대체 무슨 짓을 한 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: VeryAngry
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: VeryAngry
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: It is the will of the Great Serpent.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132340
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. INFO GROUP: COM_Barrett_AngerScene_Greet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01447D"
msgid "Do you realize what you did? You started a war with the entire Settled Systems! And for what? What reason could you possibly have to justify it?"
msgstr "네가 무슨 짓을 했는지 알고 있어? 개척 성계 전체와 전쟁을 시작했다고! 그리고 무엇을 위해? 그걸 정당화할 무슨 이유가 있을 수 있어?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Apologetic
#. PROMPT: House Dul'kehf's attention to detail will serve Dazra well.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Dul'kehf's attention to detail will serve Dazra well.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Apologetic
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132346
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01447C"
msgid "Sure. They're bean counters. But that could tie things up in regulation."
msgstr "그래. 그들은 회계사들이지. 하지만 그게 규제로 일을 묶어 버릴 수도 있어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. PROMPT: House Dul'kehf's attention to detail will serve Dazra well.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Concerned
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132346
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01447B"
msgid "One thing I appreciate about Constellation is they don't get wrapped up in red tape."
msgstr "컨스텔레이션의 좋은 점 중 하나는 그들은 형식주의에 얽매이지 않는다는 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Thinking
#. PROMPT: House Dul'kehf's attention to detail will serve Dazra well.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Thinking
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: House Ka'dic's openness with outsiders will benefit Dazra.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132346
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01447A"
msgid "Not unless that tape is a being from another universe, here to make things sticky."
msgstr "그 테이프가 다른 우주에서 온 존재라서, 일을 꼬이게 만드는 게 아니라면 말이지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. PROMPT: I think Viktor will be a good leader.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I think Viktor will be a good leader.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Concerned
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: But it did surprise me when you told them no one was fit to lead.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113233B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014477"
msgid "I hear he's got a commanding presence. Good trait for a leader, bad for a dictator."
msgstr "빅토르가 풍채는 당당하다고 들었어. 지도자에게는 좋은 자질이지만, 독재자에게는 나쁜 자질이지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. PROMPT: I don't even want to know what Dazra looks like in ten years, let alone twenty.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I don't even want to know what Dazra looks like in ten years, let alone twenty.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113233A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014476"
msgid "You can try, but you can't escape it."
msgstr "노력은 할 수 있겠지만, 피할 수는 없어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. PROMPT: I don't even want to know what Dazra looks like in ten years, let alone twenty.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: Regardless, I won't sit here and sugarcoat it. The people of Dazra have a long road ahead of it.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113233A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014475"
msgid "Even if you never step foot in Dazra again, time's a loquacious one. It'll give you the story and spare no feelings."
msgstr "네가 다시는 다즈라에 발을 들여놓지 않는다고 해도, 시간은 수다쟁이거든. 그게 너에게 이야기를 전해줄 거고, 감정 따위는 봐주지 않을 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confused
#. PROMPT: I don't want to talk about it right now.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I don't want to talk about it right now.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confused
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132335
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014474"
msgid "That's fine. We'll talk later."
msgstr "괜찮아. 나중에 얘기하자."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: The Crusade was Anasko's ambition. It was never the Serpent's will. &&& Barrett: That's the problem with omnipotent beings. Poor communication skills.|Would make things a whole lot clearer if they just stopped by and talked to you. &&& Barrett: Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed. &&& Barrett: The whims of a cosmic snake aside, House Ka'dic seems like they'd be more open to peace.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Sure. They're bean counters. But that could tie things up in regulation.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132337
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014472"
msgid "House Dul'kehf's attention to detail will serve Dazra well."
msgstr "둘케프 가문의 세심함이 다즈라에 도움이 될 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I couldn't have done it without your help. &&& Smuggler: So that's your play, huh, gassing me up. Eh, I don't care enough to stop you. &&& Smuggler: Anyway, seeing as I don't have a ship, I'm kind of out of a job.|So I was thinking, if you're looking for an extra hand, I got two. They both work well enough, for my age anyway.|But fair warning, I can't do all that "moving around and trying new things" stuff that the kids do. |Because fact is, I'm retired. Not from work, but life.
#. ALIAS: Smuggler
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Yeah, works for me.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_TaneSalavea
#. TOPIC: 01003A98
#. SCENE: DLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Smuggler_RecruitScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014471"
msgid "Let's talk about this later."
msgstr "이 얘기는 나중에 해."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Dul'kehf's attention to detail will serve Dazra well. &&& Barrett: Sure. They're bean counters. But that could tie things up in regulation.|One thing I appreciate about Constellation is they don't get wrapped up in red tape.|Not unless that tape is a being from another universe, here to make things sticky.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Hey, after what you did, they should be rolling out the red carpet for any and all outsiders.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132339
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014470"
msgid "House Ka'dic's openness with outsiders will benefit Dazra."
msgstr "카딕 가문의 개방성이 다즈라에 도움이 될 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Flirting
#. PROMPT: It was a tough choice.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: It was a tough choice.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Flirting
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132334
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01446F"
msgid "I don't know about that, dusty. On a scale of \"picking a dessert\" to \"solving quantum gravity,\" this was definitely a piece of cake."
msgstr ""
"그건 잘 모르겠는데, 두더지 양반. '디저트 고르기'부터 '양자 중력 해결하기'까지의 척도로 볼 때, 이건 확실히 식은 죽 먹기였어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: A parade would be fun. &&& Barrett: That's right! They could carry you around on a palanquin, and walk you through the city. And of course there'd be confetti. &&& Barrett: I also want to thank you for putting a halt to the Serpent's Crusade. |The last thing the Settled Systems needs is another war.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: True, but sometimes the right thing can be hard to see, especially when you have something to gain by ignoring it.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132333
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01446E"
msgid "No need to thank me. It's not as if it was a hard choice."
msgstr "고마워할 필요 없어. 어려운 선택도 아니었으니까."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: The Crusade was Anasko's ambition. It was never the Serpent's will. &&& Barrett: That's the problem with omnipotent beings. Poor communication skills.|Would make things a whole lot clearer if they just stopped by and talked to you. &&& Barrett: Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed. &&& Barrett: The whims of a cosmic snake aside, House Ka'dic seems like they'd be more open to peace.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: That's pretty messed up, but hey, it's on them for having you make that choice.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132332
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01446D"
msgid "I actually chose House Dul'kehf knowing it was the worst thing for Dazra."
msgstr "난 사실 다즈라에 최악의 선택이라는 걸 알면서도 둘케프 가문을 선택했어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: 잠깐만. 먼저 이 말부터 꼭 해야겠어. |요즘 넌 어떻게 된 거야? 그동안의 네 행동은... 그냥 잘못됐어. 천문학적으로, 우주적으로, 잘못됐다고.|난 아직 널 버릴 생각은 없어, 두더지. 내가 순진한 건지 모르겠지만, 그래도 여전히 네 가슴 속 어딘가에 마음이 있다고 믿어. 그걸 증명하겠다고 엑스레이를 찍는 일은 없도록 하자고. &&& Barrett: 
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: And what about all the lives that will be lost in the process, on both sides? Did that ever enter your thought process?
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132331
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01446C"
msgid "I did it knowing it would weaken Dazra."
msgstr "다즈라를 약화시킬 거라는 걸 알면서도 그랬어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What do you think about House Ka'dic? &&& Barrett: I hate to punt the ball here, but I'm just a tourist. I don't know enough about Va'ruun culture or politics to form an educated opinion.|And scientifically speaking, I wouldn't want to make a decision like this without a full set of data.|But gastronomically speaking, I am glad you didn't go with House Veth'aal.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I don't know them, but I do know history. And historically militant governments are a pain in the you know what.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113232E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014469"
msgid "What do you think about House Veth'aal?"
msgstr "베타알 가문에 대해 어떻게 생각해?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Ka'dic's openness with outsiders will benefit Dazra. &&& Barrett: Hey, after what you did, they should be rolling out the red carpet for any and all outsiders.|I might even hand out some flyers. Or maybe... fire them from a cannon.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Does the structure you're talking about include a barred door and no key?
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113232D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014468"
msgid "House Veth'aal will bring much needed order and structure to Dazra."
msgstr "베타알 가문은 다즈라에 절실히 필요한 질서와 체계를 가져올 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated
#. PROMPT: It doesn't matter. The decision has been made.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: It doesn't matter. The decision has been made.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Irritated
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113232C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014467"
msgid "But it DOES matter. You made these decisions. You have to own them, justify them!"
msgstr "하지만 그건 중요해. 네가 이 결정을 내렸어. 넌 그 결정을 책임지고, 정당화해야 해!"

#. PROMPT: It doesn't matter. The decision has been made.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: At the end of the day, you made a choice to start this "Serpent's Crusade."
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113232C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014466"
msgid "There's too many lives at stake for you to be so damn dismissive!"
msgstr "네가 그렇게 무책임하게 굴기에는 너무 많은 생명이 걸려 있어!"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I think Razma will be a good leader. &&& Barrett: As head of House Ka'dic, she's the spymaster, right? I've got a natural distrust of sneaky folks, built from watching years of low budget spy movies.|Still, it's worth giving her a chance. She has the connections you'd need to bring in help from outside Dazra.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I hear he's got a commanding presence. Good trait for a leader, bad for a dictator.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132329
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014465"
msgid "I think Viktor will be a good leader."
msgstr "빅토르가 훌륭한 지도자가 될 것 같아."

#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113232B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014461"
msgid "First off, I just want to say, heck of a job saving Dazra. That was a tough situation to navigate, and you did it with aplomb."
msgstr "우선, 다즈라를 구한 거 정말 대단하다고 말하고 싶어. 헤쳐나가기 힘든 상황이었는데, 훌륭하게 해냈어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: A parade would be fun.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113232B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014460"
msgid "A pat on the back isn't nearly enough. I hope they throw you a parade."
msgstr "등을 토닥여주는 걸로는 턱없이 부족해. 퍼레이드라도 열어 줬으면 좋겠는데."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: A parade would be fun. &&& Barrett: That's right! They could carry you around on a palanquin, and walk you through the city. And of course there'd be confetti. &&& Barrett: I also want to thank you for putting a halt to the Serpent's Crusade. |The last thing the Settled Systems needs is another war.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: That's fine. We'll talk later.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132328
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01445F"
msgid "I don't want to talk about it right now."
msgstr "지금은 그 일에 대해 이야기하고 싶지 않아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I'm an outsider. The fact they even gave me a vote is ridiculous. &&& Barrett: You've got a point. But when people are vying for a throne, sometimes an outsider's the only person who can be objective. &&& Barrett: Well, either way, I won't waste your brain cells on the what-ifs. The fact is you got rid of the vortex, and saved Dazra.|As for the whole "choosing a leader" thing, time will tell if you made the right choice.|Give it maybe twenty years and you'll start to see the results.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: You can try, but you can't escape it. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132327
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01445E"
msgid "I don't even want to know what Dazra looks like in ten years, let alone twenty."
msgstr "10년 후는 고사하고 20년 후의 다즈라가 어떤 모습일지 알고 싶지도 않아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. PROMPT: I don't know, another war might've been interesting and good for the economy.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I don't know, another war might've been interesting and good for the economy.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132325
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01445D"
msgid "That's the parable of the broken window. Sure, it benefits the window fixers, but not the person paying for it."
msgstr "그게 바로 깨진 유리창의 우화야. 물론, 유리창 수리공에게는 이익이겠지만, 그걸 지불하는 사람에게는 아니지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: The Crusade was Anasko's ambition. It was never the Serpent's will. &&& Barrett: That's the problem with omnipotent beings. Poor communication skills.|Would make things a whole lot clearer if they just stopped by and talked to you. &&& Barrett: Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed. &&& Barrett: The whims of a cosmic snake aside, House Ka'dic seems like they'd be more open to peace.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: From what I understand, he's a taskmaster.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113231E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01445C"
msgid "I think Hasmak will be a good leader."
msgstr "해즈막이 훌륭한 지도자가 될 것 같아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I actually chose House Ka'dic knowing it was the worst thing for Dazra. &&& Barrett: That's pretty messed up, but hey, it's on them for having you make that choice.|But I do know you make a damn persuasive argument.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Well you'll get no argument from me. Not sure the citizens of Dazra are prepared for what's coming though.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132323
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01445B"
msgid "I actually chose House Veth'aal knowing it was the worst thing for Dazra."
msgstr "난 사실 다즈라에 최악의 선택이라는 걸 알면서도 베타알 가문을 선택했어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: 잠깐만. 먼저 이 말부터 꼭 해야겠어. |요즘 넌 어떻게 된 거야? 그동안의 네 행동은... 그냥 잘못됐어. 천문학적으로, 우주적으로, 잘못됐다고.|난 아직 널 버릴 생각은 없어, 두더지. 내가 순진한 건지 모르겠지만, 그래도 여전히 네 가슴 속 어딘가에 마음이 있다고 믿어. 그걸 증명하겠다고 엑스레이를 찍는 일은 없도록 하자고. &&& Barrett: 
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Maybe not at the start. But they're militant, focused, and fiercely determined.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113231D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01445A"
msgid "It won't be a full scale war."
msgstr "전면전은 아닐 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: You've got a point. But when people are vying for a throne, sometimes an outsider's the only person who can be objective.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113231C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014459"
msgid "Well, either way, I won't waste your brain cells on the what-ifs. The fact is you got rid of the vortex, and saved Dazra."
msgstr "어쨌든, 네 머리를 '만약’이라는 생각으로 낭비하게 하진 않을 거야. 중요한 건 네가 볼텍스를 제거하고 다즈라를 구했다는 거야."

#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113231C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014458"
msgid "As for the whole \"choosing a leader\" thing, time will tell if you made the right choice."
msgstr "그리고 '지도자 선택’에 관해서는, 네가 옳은 선택을 했는지는 시간이 말해줄 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I'm an outsider. The fact they even gave me a vote is ridiculous. &&& Barrett: You've got a point. But when people are vying for a throne, sometimes an outsider's the only person who can be objective. &&& Barrett: Well, either way, I won't waste your brain cells on the what-ifs. The fact is you got rid of the vortex, and saved Dazra.|As for the whole "choosing a leader" thing, time will tell if you made the right choice.|Give it maybe twenty years and you'll start to see the results.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: You and me both. But something like this doesn't go away in a year.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132320
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014457"
msgid "For the sake of Dazra, I hope to see improvement sooner than that."
msgstr "다즈라를 위해서, 그보다 더 빨리 개선됐으면 좋겠어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. PROMPT: I actually chose House Veth'aal knowing it was the worst thing for Dazra.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I actually chose House Veth'aal knowing it was the worst thing for Dazra.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: But it did surprise me when you told them no one was fit to lead.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113231F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014456"
msgid "Well you'll get no argument from me. Not sure the citizens of Dazra are prepared for what's coming though."
msgstr "그건 나도 동의해. 하지만 다즈라 시민들이 앞으로 닥칠 일을 감당할 준비가 되었는지는 잘 모르겠어."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I'm an outsider. The fact they even gave me a vote is ridiculous. &&& Barrett: You've got a point. But when people are vying for a throne, sometimes an outsider's the only person who can be objective. &&& Barrett: Well, either way, I won't waste your brain cells on the what-ifs. The fact is you got rid of the vortex, and saved Dazra.|As for the whole "choosing a leader" thing, time will tell if you made the right choice.|Give it maybe twenty years and you'll start to see the results.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Ha, you're traveling forward right now. Sure it's a slow ride, but you can enjoy the view.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132317
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014452"
msgid "I can travel to other dimensions, but not forward in time."
msgstr "난 다른 차원으로 이동할 수 있지만, 시간 여행은 할 수 없어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. PROMPT: For the sake of Dazra, I hope to see improvement sooner than that.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: For the sake of Dazra, I hope to see improvement sooner than that.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113231B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01444D"
msgid "You and me both. But something like this doesn't go away in a year."
msgstr "너나 나나 마찬가지야. 하지만 이런 일은 1년 만에 사라지지 않아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. PROMPT: For the sake of Dazra, I hope to see improvement sooner than that.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Concerned
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: Regardless, I won't sit here and sugarcoat it. The people of Dazra have a long road ahead of it.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113231B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01444C"
msgid "And even if the city is restored, the scars will last generations."
msgstr "그리고 도시가 복구된다고 해도, 상처는 몇 세대 동안 지속될 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: House Dul'kehf's attention to detail will serve Dazra well.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113231A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01444A"
msgid "The whims of a cosmic snake aside, House Ka'dic seems like they'd be more open to peace."
msgstr "우주 뱀의 변덕은 제쳐두고, 카딕 가문은 평화에 더 열려 있는 것 같아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Irritated
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: House Dul'kehf's attention to detail will serve Dazra well.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113231A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014449"
msgid "The whims of a cosmic snake aside, House Dul'kehf seems like they'd be more open to trade with the Settled Systems."
msgstr "우주 뱀의 변덕은 제쳐두고, 둘케프 가문은 개척 성계와의 교역에 더 열려 있는 것 같아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Concerned
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: House Dul'kehf's attention to detail will serve Dazra well.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113231A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014448"
msgid "I'm just not sure House Veth'aal's militant attitude makes them less or more susceptible to the whims of a cosmic snake."
msgstr "베타알 가문의 호전적인 태도가 우주 뱀의 변덕에 덜 휘둘리게 할지, 더 휘둘리게 할지는 잘 모르겠어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Suspicious
#. PROMPT: I think Razma will be a good leader.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I think Razma will be a good leader.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Suspicious
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132316
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014447"
msgid "As head of House Ka'dic, she's the spymaster, right? I've got a natural distrust of sneaky folks, built from watching years of low budget spy movies."
msgstr ""
"카딕 가문의 수장으로서, 라즈마는 스파이 마스터잖아? 수년간 저예산 스파이 영화를 봐서 그런가. 은밀한 사람들은 자연스럽게 불신하게 "
"되더라고."

#. PROMPT: I think Razma will be a good leader.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I think Viktor will be a good leader.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132316
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014446"
msgid "Still, it's worth giving her a chance. She has the connections you'd need to bring in help from outside Dazra."
msgstr "그래도, 라즈마에게 기회를 줘 볼 만한 가치는 있어. 라즈마는 다즈라 밖에서 도움을 줄 수 있는 인맥을 가지고 있으니까."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. PROMPT: It will take much longer for the wounds to truly heal.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: It will take much longer for the wounds to truly heal.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Concerned
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: Regardless, I won't sit here and sugarcoat it. The people of Dazra have a long road ahead of it.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132315
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014445"
msgid "Agreed. If history is our teacher here, major cataclysms come with deep wounds and emotional scars."
msgstr "동의해. 역사가 우리에게 가르쳐 주듯이, 대격변은 깊은 상처와 정서적 흉터를 동반하지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. PROMPT: No need to thank me. It's not as if it was a hard choice.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: No need to thank me. It's not as if it was a hard choice.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113230E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014444"
msgid "True, but sometimes the right thing can be hard to see, especially when you have something to gain by ignoring it."
msgstr "맞아, 하지만 때로는 옳은 일을 보기가 어려울 수 있어. 특히 그걸 무시함으로써 얻을 게 있을 때는 더욱 그렇지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. PROMPT: No need to thank me. It's not as if it was a hard choice.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113230E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014443"
msgid "And you spent a lot of time in Dazra. Who knows how that might've shifted your perspective."
msgstr "그리고 넌 다즈라에서 많은 시간을 보냈어. 그게 네 관점을 어떻게 바꿨을지 누가 알겠어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: Are you kidding me? That's a cop out. |This isn't some political argument with no answer. This is the difference between right and wrong, life and death.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Angry
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: I want you to open your eyes and see the consequences of that choice. And if you can't, then I can't be a part of it.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132313
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014442"
msgid "At the end of the day, you made a choice to start this \"Serpent's Crusade.\""
msgstr "결국, 이 '뱀의 성전’을 시작하기로 선택한 건 너야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: The Crusade was Anasko's ambition. It was never the Serpent's will. &&& Barrett: That's the problem with omnipotent beings. Poor communication skills.|Would make things a whole lot clearer if they just stopped by and talked to you. &&& Barrett: Either way, I hope the new leadership in Dazra is just as level headed. &&& Barrett: The whims of a cosmic snake aside, House Ka'dic seems like they'd be more open to peace.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I hate to punt the ball here, but I'm just a tourist. I don't know enough about Va'ruun culture or politics to form an educated opinion.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132312
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014441"
msgid "What do you think about House Dul'kehf?"
msgstr "둘케프 가문에 대해 어떻게 생각해?"

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I didn't put much thought into the choice, to be honest.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: But it did surprise me when you told them no one was fit to lead.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132311
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014440"
msgid "Well that explains a lot. Might've been better off putting the names in a hat."
msgstr "그거 참 잘됐네. 차라리 모자에 이름을 넣고 뽑는 게 더 나았을지도 모르겠어."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What do you think about House Dul'kehf? &&& Barrett: I hate to punt the ball here, but I'm just a tourist. I don't know enough about Va'ruun culture or politics to form an educated opinion.|And scientifically speaking, I wouldn't want to make a decision like this without a full set of data.|But gastronomically speaking, I am glad you didn't go with House Veth'aal.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I hate to punt the ball here, but I'm just a tourist. I don't know enough about Va'ruun culture or politics to form an educated opinion.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113230F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01443F"
msgid "What do you think about House Ka'dic?"
msgstr "카딕 가문에 대해 어떻게 생각해?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated
#. PROMPT: House Ka'dic's openness with outsiders will benefit Dazra.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Ka'dic's openness with outsiders will benefit Dazra.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Irritated
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132314
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01443E"
msgid "Hey, after what you did, they should be rolling out the red carpet for any and all outsiders."
msgstr "이봐, 네가 한 짓을 생각하면, 그들이 모든 이방인들에게 레드 카펫을 깔아 줘야 마땅하지."

#. PROMPT: House Ka'dic's openness with outsiders will benefit Dazra.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: House Veth'aal will bring much needed order and structure to Dazra.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132314
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01443D"
msgid "I might even hand out some flyers. Or maybe... fire them from a cannon."
msgstr "전단지나 좀 돌릴까 봐. 아니면... 대포로 쏴 버릴까."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Smirk
#. PROMPT: I can travel to other dimensions, but not forward in time.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I can travel to other dimensions, but not forward in time.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Smirk
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: Regardless, I won't sit here and sugarcoat it. The people of Dazra have a long road ahead of it.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113230D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01443C"
msgid "Ha, you're traveling forward right now. Sure it's a slow ride, but you can enjoy the view."
msgstr "하, 넌 지금 시간 여행을 하고 있어. 물론 느린 여행이지만, 경치는 즐길 수 있잖아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: A parade would be fun. &&& Barrett: That's right! They could carry you around on a palanquin, and walk you through the city. And of course there'd be confetti. &&& Barrett: I also want to thank you for putting a halt to the Serpent's Crusade. |The last thing the Settled Systems needs is another war.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: That's the parable of the broken window. Sure, it benefits the window fixers, but not the person paying for it.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132307
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01443B"
msgid "I don't know, another war might've been interesting and good for the economy."
msgstr "모르겠어, 또 다른 전쟁은 흥미롭고 경제에도 좋을 수 있었을 텐데."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I'm an outsider. The fact they even gave me a vote is ridiculous. &&& Barrett: You've got a point. But when people are vying for a throne, sometimes an outsider's the only person who can be objective. &&& Barrett: Well, either way, I won't waste your brain cells on the what-ifs. The fact is you got rid of the vortex, and saved Dazra.|As for the whole "choosing a leader" thing, time will tell if you made the right choice.|Give it maybe twenty years and you'll start to see the results.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: It is what scholars do. Even the physical sciences have gone from objective truths to having to deal with the more unpredicatable quantum side of things.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 0113230B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014438"
msgid "I personally love debating what-ifs. Woulda, shoulda, coulda is also a favorite pastime of mine."
msgstr "난 개인적으로 '만약’에 대해 토론하는 걸 좋아해. ‘했더라면’, ‘해야 했는데’, '할 수 있었는데’도 내가 가장 좋아하는 것들이지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: Ha, you're traveling forward right now. Sure it's a slow ride, but you can enjoy the view.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132308
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014437"
msgid "Regardless, I won't sit here and sugarcoat it. The people of Dazra have a long road ahead of it."
msgstr "어쨌든, 난 여기서 미사여구를 늘어놓지는 않을 거야. 다즈라 사람들에게는 앞으로 갈 길이 멀어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132308
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014436"
msgid "They're going to have to make foundational decisions regarding everything from infrastructure to immigration to their core religious beliefs."
msgstr "그들은 기반 시설부터 이민, 핵심 종교적 신념에 이르기까지 모든 것에 대한 근본적인 결정을 내려야 할 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132308
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014435"
msgid "Let's hope this first push sends them on the right path."
msgstr "이 첫 번째 추진력이 그들을 올바른 길로 인도하기를 바라자."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. PROMPT: I think Hasmak will be a good leader.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I think Hasmak will be a good leader.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Concerned
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132309
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014434"
msgid "From what I understand, he's a taskmaster."
msgstr "내가 알기로, 해즈막은 엄격한 감독관이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. PROMPT: I think Hasmak will be a good leader.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132309
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014433"
msgid "Not my cup of tea. Rules and regulations are bad words in my dictionary."
msgstr "내 취향은 아니야. 규칙과 규제는 내 사전에 없는 말들이지."

#. PROMPT: I think Hasmak will be a good leader.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I think Razma will be a good leader.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132309
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014432"
msgid "But far large scale projects, it's usually for the best."
msgstr "하지만 대규모 프로젝트의 경우, 대개는 그게 최선이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: A parade would be fun. &&& Barrett: That's right! They could carry you around on a palanquin, and walk you through the city. And of course there'd be confetti. &&& Barrett: I also want to thank you for putting a halt to the Serpent's Crusade. |The last thing the Settled Systems needs is another war.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: That's the problem with omnipotent beings. Poor communication skills.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132306
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014431"
msgid "The Crusade was Anasko's ambition. It was never the Serpent's will."
msgstr "성전은 아나스코의 야망이었어. 그건 결코 뱀의 뜻이 아니었어."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Let's just agree to disagree. &&& Barrett: Are you kidding me? That's a cop out. |This isn't some political argument with no answer. This is the difference between right and wrong, life and death. &&& Barrett: At the end of the day, you made a choice to start this "Serpent's Crusade." &&& Barrett: I want you to open your eyes and see the consequences of that choice. And if you can't, then I can't be a part of it.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I'd really like to believe that...
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132305
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014430"
msgid "[Second Chance] I didn't realize the consequences of that choice. I'll try to make better decisions from now on."
msgstr "[두 번째 기회] 그 선택의 결과를 몰랐어. 앞으로는 더 나은 결정을 내리도록 노력할게."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated but also willing to believe. / Irritated
#. PROMPT: [Second Chance] I didn't realize the consequences of that choice. I'll try to make better decisions from now on. 
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: [Second Chance] I didn't realize the consequences of that choice. I'll try to make better decisions from now on. 
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Irritated
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: We've been through so much, and are on this journey together.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132304
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_System_AngerSceneSerpentsCrusade
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01442F"
msgid "I'd really like to believe that..."
msgstr "정말 그렇게 믿고 싶어..."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. PROMPT: I personally love debating what-ifs. Woulda, shoulda, coulda is also a favorite pastime of mine.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I personally love debating what-ifs. Woulda, shoulda, coulda is also a favorite pastime of mine.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Neutral
