#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01442E"
msgid "It is what scholars do. Even the physical sciences have gone from objective truths to having to deal with the more unpredicatable quantum side of things."
msgstr "그게 학자들이 하는 일이야. 심지어 물리학조차도 객관적인 진실에서 벗어나 더 예측 불가능한 양자역학적인 측면을 다루게 되었지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Question
#. PROMPT: I personally love debating what-ifs. Woulda, shoulda, coulda is also a favorite pastime of mine.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Question
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: Regardless, I won't sit here and sugarcoat it. The people of Dazra have a long road ahead of it.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132302
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01442D"
msgid "Is Schrodinger's cat dead, alive, or both? What happens when things go unobserved?"
msgstr "슈뢰딩거의 고양이는 죽었을까, 살았을까, 아니면 둘 다일까? 관찰되지 않으면 어떤 일이 벌어질까?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Player
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I'm an outsider. The fact they even gave me a vote is ridiculous. &&& Barrett: You've got a point. But when people are vying for a throne, sometimes an outsider's the only person who can be objective. &&& Barrett: Well, either way, I won't waste your brain cells on the what-ifs. The fact is you got rid of the vortex, and saved Dazra.|As for the whole "choosing a leader" thing, time will tell if you made the right choice.|Give it maybe twenty years and you'll start to see the results.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Player
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Agreed. If history is our teacher here, major cataclysms come with deep wounds and emotional scars.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 01132301
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01442C"
msgid "It will take much longer for the wounds to truly heal."
msgstr "상처가 진정으로 치유되려면 훨씬 더 오랜 시간이 걸릴 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Veth'aal will bring much needed order and structure to Dazra. &&& Barrett: Does the structure you're talking about include a barred door and no key?|Because that's what House Veth'aal likes to do. &&& Barrett: But it did surprise me when you told them no one was fit to lead.|I know you're not afraid of making hard decisions, so maybe there was another reason you abstained from making a choice.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: You've got a point. But when people are vying for a throne, sometimes an outsider's the only person who can be objective.
