#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01442B"
msgid "I'm an outsider. The fact they even gave me a vote is ridiculous."
msgstr "난 이방인이야. 그들이 나에게 투표권을 줬다는 사실조차 우스워."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Thinking / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: I'm an outsider. The fact they even gave me a vote is ridiculous.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I'm an outsider. The fact they even gave me a vote is ridiculous.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Thinking
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Barrett: Well, either way, I won't waste your brain cells on the what-ifs. The fact is you got rid of the vortex, and saved Dazra.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 011322FE
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01442A"
msgid "You've got a point. But when people are vying for a throne, sometimes an outsider's the only person who can be objective."
msgstr "일리가 있네. 하지만 사람들이 왕좌를 놓고 경쟁할 때는, 때로는 이방인만이 객관적일 수 있는 유일한 사람이지."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Barrett: Does the structure you're talking about include a barred door and no key?|Because that's what House Veth'aal likes to do.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 011322FD
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014429"
msgid "But it did surprise me when you told them no one was fit to lead."
msgstr "하지만 네가 그들에게 아무도 지도자에 적합하지 않다고 말했을 때는 놀랐어."

#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: NPCMBarrett
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I'm an outsider. The fact they even gave me a vote is ridiculous.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 011322FD
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014428"
msgid "I know you're not afraid of making hard decisions, so maybe there was another reason you abstained from making a choice."
msgstr "네가 어려운 결정을 내리는 걸 두려워하지 않는다는 걸 알고 있으니까, 아마도 네가 선택을 포기한 다른 이유가 있었을 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: House Veth'aal will bring much needed order and structure to Dazra. &&& Barrett: Does the structure you're talking about include a barred door and no key?|Because that's what House Veth'aal likes to do. &&& Barrett: But it did surprise me when you told them no one was fit to lead.|I know you're not afraid of making hard decisions, so maybe there was another reason you abstained from making a choice.
#. ALIAS: Barrett
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: That's a good point. But maybe your hand doesn't have to be a crutch. It can be a boost.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_COM_Companion_Barrett
#. TOPIC: 011322FC
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_COM_Barrett_QuestEvent_MQ06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "014427"
msgid "I won't always be there to hold their hand. They're doomed."
msgstr "내가 항상 그들의 손을 잡고 있을 수는 없잖아. 그들은 파멸할 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: I won't always be there to hold their hand. They're doomed.
