#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013BB2"
msgid "I appreciate that someone around here is eager to get to work."
msgstr "열심히 일해 주려는 사람이 있다니, 정말 고맙구만."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Ekris: And Hasmak, the new Elder of House Dul'kehf... He has been distant, guarded. He claims to have vital information about an important component of the experiment, but has withheld it until now.
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Ekris: And, I may have something that can help you on whatever trials the Serpent puts before you as we navigate this.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ02
#. TOPIC: 011189E9
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ02_Stage1000_EkrisScene01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013BB1"
msgid "Help me get what we need, and we will see what we can do for the Speaker, and for House Va'ruun."
msgstr "필요한 걸 구해준다면, 우리가 대변자님과 바룬 가문을 위해 뭘 할 수 있을지 알아보겠네."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: No use complaining about the past. Time to move forward. &&& ...  &&& Ekris: I believe I've done enough complaining for now. Time to get to work. &&& Ekris: If you're here, the Council has likely sent word to the Houses that it's time to stop the infighting. I doubt it will be enough. &&& Ekris: I need to oversee construction here, make sure things are built to specifications. If you could follow up with the Houses, that may speed up the process.
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Lately we have all needed to be comfortable with doing things outside our usual responsibilities. You are one of us now, and are no different. All Must Serve, remember?
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ02
#. TOPIC: 011189EE
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ02_Stage1000_EkrisScene01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013BB0"
msgid "I shouldn't have to do that."
msgstr "반드시 해야 하는 건 아니잖아요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Smirk / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: I shouldn't have to do that.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I shouldn't have to do that.
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Smirk
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Ekris: House Veth'aal owes us access codes for the city power grid. It's the only way to guarantee enough power to activate the device.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ02
#. TOPIC: 011189ED
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ02_Stage1000_EkrisScene01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013BAF"
msgid "Lately we have all needed to be comfortable with doing things outside our usual responsibilities. You are one of us now, and are no different. All Must Serve, remember?"
msgstr ""
"지금은 다들 평소에 하던 일과는 다른 일을 맡는 데 익숙해져야 하네. 자네도 이제 우리 일원이니, 예외가 아니야. 모두가 섬겨야 한다. "
"기억하지?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: No use complaining about the past. Time to move forward. &&& ...  &&& Ekris: I believe I've done enough complaining for now. Time to get to work. &&& Ekris: If you're here, the Council has likely sent word to the Houses that it's time to stop the infighting. I doubt it will be enough. &&& Ekris: I need to oversee construction here, make sure things are built to specifications. If you could follow up with the Houses, that may speed up the process.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: The first convert in generations? The only one to have heard from the Speaker since the disaster? Oh, I think they will listen.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ02
#. TOPIC: 011189F2
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ02_Stage1000_EkrisScene01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013BAE"
msgid "I doubt they'll listen to me."
msgstr "제 말을 들어줄 것 같지가 않은데요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Thinking / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Ekris: House Ka'dic was supposed to provide a young scientist named Sahima to help me. She had at least some experience with the original Citadel experiment. No idea why they refuse to send her.
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Thinking
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Ekris: Help me get what we need, and we will see what we can do for the Speaker, and for House Va'ruun.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ02
#. TOPIC: 011189EA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ02_Stage1000_EkrisScene01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013BAD"
msgid "And Hasmak, the new Elder of House Dul'kehf... He has been distant, guarded. He claims to have vital information about an important component of the experiment, but has withheld it until now."
msgstr ""
"그리고 둘케프 가문의 새 장로가 된 해즈막은... 멀찍이 거리를 둔 채 경계하고 있지. 해즈막은 실험의 주요 구성 요소에 대한 중요 "
"정보를 가지고 있다고 주장하지만, 지금까지 그걸 숨기고 있어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Ekris: The first convert in generations? The only one to have heard from the Speaker since the disaster? Oh, I think they will listen.
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Ekris: House Ka'dic was supposed to provide a young scientist named Sahima to help me. She had at least some experience with the original Citadel experiment. No idea why they refuse to send her.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ02
#. TOPIC: 011189EC
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ02_Stage1000_EkrisScene01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013BAC"
msgid "House Veth'aal owes us access codes for the city power grid. It's the only way to guarantee enough power to activate the device."
msgstr "베타알 가문은 도시 전력망 접속 코드를 넘겨주기로 했었네. 그게 있어야만 장치를 작동시킬 전력을 충분히 확보할 수 있지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: No, but maybe I can help you. Seems like you've hit some trouble. &&& Qisrani: "Trouble" only begins to describe it. &&& Qisrani: It's about the supply shortage. There may be a reason for it, beyond the cataclysm itself.|A week ago my cousin, Ukaru, came to my office concerned about a series of lost shipments. |He was certain someone was using the tragedy as cover, to steal supplies and route them to our enemies.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Yes. But given the seriousness of the accusation, the proof must be irrefutable.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS01
#. TOPIC: 01118135
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001MS01_Scene_020_Greeting
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013BAB"
msgid "Doing so would be treason."
msgstr "그런 짓을 하면 반역 행위가 될 겁니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Doing so would be treason.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Doing so would be treason.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFQisraniDulkehf
#. FACE: Serious
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Qisrani: So I told my cousin to return with more evidence, and when I didn't hear back, I assumed that was the end of it. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS01
#. TOPIC: 01118134
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001MS01_Scene_020_Greeting
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013BAA"
msgid "Yes. But given the seriousness of the accusation, the proof must be irrefutable."
msgstr "네, 하지만 혐의가 심각한 만큼, 증거는 반박할 수 없는 수준이어야 해요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Using the tragedy as cover seems especially low.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Using the tragedy as cover seems especially low.
#. ALIAS: Qisrani
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFQisraniDulkehf
#. FACE: Serious
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Qisrani: So I told my cousin to return with more evidence, and when I didn't hear back, I assumed that was the end of it. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS01
#. TOPIC: 01118132
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001MS01_Scene_020_Greeting
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013BA9"
msgid "Agreed. It is difficult to believe, and as such, the proof must be ironclad."
msgstr "동의해요. 믿기 어려운 일이니, 증거는 철통같아야 해요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: No, but maybe I can help you. Seems like you've hit some trouble. &&& Qisrani: "Trouble" only begins to describe it. &&& Qisrani: It's about the supply shortage. There may be a reason for it, beyond the cataclysm itself.|A week ago my cousin, Ukaru, came to my office concerned about a series of lost shipments. |He was certain someone was using the tragedy as cover, to steal supplies and route them to our enemies.
