#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_13_PoisonedNoOne
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01341D"
msgid "Amila is dead because Borhal killed him. I had nothing to do with this."
msgstr "아밀라가 죽은 건 보할이 살해해서 그런 거고요. 저랑은 아무 상관 없습니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Amila is dead because Borhal killed him. I had nothing to do with this.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Amila is dead because Borhal killed him. I had nothing to do with this.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDanikaHagan
#. FACE: Irritated
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Borhal: Enough, Danika! They are right. The only one here with blood on their hands is me. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B80E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_13_PoisonedNoOne
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01341C"
msgid "But you had the chance to stop this madness!"
msgstr "하지만 당신한테 이 미친 짓을 막을 기회가 있었잖아요!"

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: It's all right, Amila. It was you or him.  &&& ...  &&& Danika: Ugh! This... this should not have happened!|What have you done? You were supposed to tranquilize them both! You were supposed to scuttle the duel!  &&& Amila: Scuttle the duel? What is she talking about? &&& Danika: Fool... Borhal is dead because of you.
#. ALIAS: Danika
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Do not put this on me! What you did was... it was murder!
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110ED42
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_12_AmilaSurvived
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01341B"
msgid "Your anger is completely misguided. You should have done more to end this."
msgstr "엉뚱한 사람한테 화를 내고 계시네요. 이런 일이 일어나지 않도록 당신이 더 최선을 다했어야죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Your anger is completely misguided. You should have done more to end this.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Your anger is completely misguided. You should have done more to end this.
#. ALIAS: Danika
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDanikaHagan
#. FACE: Irritated
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Borhal: Stop it, Danika. They did nothing wrong. This... tranquilizer would have only delayed the inevitable, anyway. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B80C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_13_PoisonedNoOne
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01341A"
msgid "You..."
msgstr "당신..."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: It had to be done, Borhal.  &&& ...  &&& Danika: Ugh! This... this should not have happened!|What have you done? You were supposed to tranquilize them both! You were supposed to scuttle the duel!  &&& Borhal: What?  &&& Danika: Fool... Amila is dead because of you.
#. ALIAS: Danika
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: It would have worked. I know it would have worked!
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B80B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_13_PoisonedNoOne
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013419"
msgid "There's no guarantee the tranquilizer would have even worked."
msgstr "어차피 진정제가 통할 거라는 보장도 없었잖아요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated / to Danika
#. PROMPT: Amila is dead because Borhal killed him. I had nothing to do with this.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Amila is dead because Borhal killed him. I had nothing to do with this. &&& Danika: But you had the chance to stop this madness!
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMBorhalAdlam
#. FACE: Irritated
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Danika: This is... I am done. Tend to your brother yourself.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B809
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_13_PoisonedNoOne
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013418"
msgid "Enough, Danika! They are right. The only one here with blood on their hands is me."
msgstr "그만해라, 다니카! 저 사람 말이 맞아. 여기서 목숨을 앗아간 자는 오직 나뿐인 거네."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: There's no guarantee the tranquilizer would have even worked.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: There's no guarantee the tranquilizer would have even worked.
#. ALIAS: Danika
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDanikaHagan
#. FACE: Irritated
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Borhal: Even if it had worked, the duel would be incomplete. I would have made sure to continue with different seconds.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B80A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_13_PoisonedNoOne
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013417"
msgid "It would have worked. I know it would have worked!"
msgstr "약효가 있었을 거라고요. 약효가 있을 거라 확신했다고요!"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Danika
#. PROMPT: Your anger is completely misguided. You should have done more to end this.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Your anger is completely misguided. You should have done more to end this. &&& Danika: You...
#. ALIAS: Borhal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMBorhalAdlam
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Danika: This is... I am done. Tend to your brother yourself.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B808
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_13_PoisonedNoOne
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013416"
msgid "Stop it, Danika. They did nothing wrong. This... tranquilizer would have only delayed the inevitable, anyway."
msgstr "그만해라, 다니카. 저 사람은 아무 잘못 없다. 진정제는... 이미 예정된 결과를 늦추는 효과만 일으켰겠지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated / to Danika
#. PROMPT: There's no guarantee the tranquilizer would have even worked.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: There's no guarantee the tranquilizer would have even worked. &&& Danika: It would have worked. I know it would have worked!
#. ALIAS: Borhal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMBorhalAdlam
#. FACE: Irritated
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Danika: This is... I am done. Tend to your brother yourself.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B807
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_13_PoisonedNoOne
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013415"
msgid "Even if it had worked, the duel would be incomplete. I would have made sure to continue with different seconds."
msgstr "그게 통했어도, 결투는 끝나지 않았을 테지. 바로 다른 입회인들을 구했을 거라네."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Borhal: Enough, Danika! They are right. The only one here with blood on their hands is me.  &&& Danika: This is... I am done. Tend to your brother yourself.
#. ALIAS: Borhal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMBorhalAdlam
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Borhal: Your duty as a second has ended. You served Amila honorably, and I thank you for that. Now, I am sure you are eager for your promised payment. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B806
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_13_PoisonedNoOne
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013414"
msgid "Do not let Danika shame you. What you did was honorable. Amila accepted the duel, and you let it play out fairly. You did nothing wrong."
msgstr ""
"다니카의 말에 상처받지 말게. 자네는 명예로운 선택을 내렸어. 아밀라는 결투를 받아들였고 공정하게 이루어지도록 했지. 잘못한 것이 없네."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry / to Borhal
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Danika: But you had the chance to stop this madness! &&& Borhal: Enough, Danika! They are right. The only one here with blood on their hands is me. 
#. ALIAS: Danika
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDanikaHagan
#. FACE: Angry
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Borhal: Do not let Danika shame you. What you did was honorable. Amila accepted the duel, and you let it play out fairly. You did nothing wrong.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B805
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_13_PoisonedNoOne
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013413"
msgid "This is... I am done. Tend to your brother yourself."
msgstr "이건... 난 몰라요. 당신 형제는 알아서 챙기세요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Danika: Thank the Great Serpent, you did it. The tranquilizer worked, and you saved them both. Thank you for trusting me.
#. ALIAS: Danika
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I have faith that the Great Serpent will open their hearts to each other.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B804
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_12_BothBrothersSurvivedDanikaFollowUp
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013412"
msgid "How do you know they won't just duel each other again?"
msgstr "왜 나중에 다시 서로 결투를 벌이지 않을 거라 확신하는 거죠?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: How do you know they won't just duel each other again?
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: How do you know they won't just duel each other again?
#. ALIAS: Danika
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDanikaHagan
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B803
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_12_BothBrothersSurvivedDanikaFollowUp
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013411"
msgid "I have faith that the Great Serpent will open their hearts to each other."
msgstr "위대한 뱀께서 서로의 마음이 서로에게 닿도록 인도하실 거라 믿거든요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: How do you know they won't just duel each other again?
#. ALIAS: Danika
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDanikaHagan
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Danika: I'm glad your plan worked.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B803
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_12_BothBrothersSurvivedDanikaFollowUp
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013410"
msgid "He will show them that the pain from the tranquilizer would be dwarfed by humiliation and guilt, had the duel ended in bloodshed."
msgstr "그분이라면, 결투가 피바다로 끝났다면, 진정제의 고통 따위는 비교도 안 될 수치심과 죄책감을 내려 주셨겠죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Will they be okay? &&& Danika: What? From the tranquilizer? They will sleep a few days and be fine, I expect...|They may suffer a bit, but it is a far better alternative to being stabbed to death.
#. ALIAS: Danika
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Hmmph, some of Amila's pessimism seems to have rubbed off on you. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B802
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_12_BothBrothersSurvivedDanikaFollowUp
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01340F"
msgid "If you say so. I'm not so sure that this is the end."
msgstr "그렇게 말할 수야 있겠죠. 이게 끝은 아닐 것 같지만요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: If you say so. I'm not so sure that this is the end.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: If you say so. I'm not so sure that this is the end.
#. ALIAS: Danika
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDanikaHagan
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Danika: I want to thank you. You trusted me, and because of you, the brothers - my friends - are both alive. They are imbeciles, but better people than they seem. I am grateful for you.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B801
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_12_BothBrothersSurvivedDanikaFollowUp
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01340E"
msgid "Hmmph, some of Amila's pessimism seems to have rubbed off on you."
msgstr "흐음. 아밀라의 비관적인 사고방식이 당신에게도 옮았나 보군요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: That wasn't the happy ending I was expecting. &&& Danika: Nonsense. You've made the right choice. |Their egos are bruised, but deep down, they are both relieved. |Come what may, we have narrowly avoided a bloodbath today. If they are stupid enough to try again, we will find another way to stop it.|But I doubt that day will come.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Me too.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B800
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_12_BothBrothersSurvivedDanikaFollowUp
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01340D"
msgid "I'm glad your plan worked."
msgstr "당신이 계획한 대로 이루어져서 다행이네요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Friendly / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: I'm glad your plan worked.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I'm glad your plan worked.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDanikaHagan
#. FACE: Friendly
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Danika: I want to thank you. You trusted me, and because of you, the brothers - my friends - are both alive. They are imbeciles, but better people than they seem. I am grateful for you.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FF
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_12_BothBrothersSurvivedDanikaFollowUp
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01340C"
msgid "Me too."
msgstr "저도요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Stern
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFRazmaKadic
#. FACE: Stern
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVDazra
#. TOPIC: 0102FD8A
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_MQ_RazmaHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "01340B"
msgid "What is it now?"
msgstr "이번엔 무슨 일인가?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious / to Borhal
#. ALIAS: Danika
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDanikaHagan
#. FACE: Serious
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Amila: Too late, Danika. He has issued his challenge.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 010655C7
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_03_QuestIntro
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01340A"
msgid "There is already so much death in the city. What good would this do? There has to be another way."
msgstr "이미 도시에 죽은 사람들이 얼마나 많은데. 대체 이게 무슨 소용이 있겠어요? 다른 방법이 있을 거예요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry / to Borhal
#. ALIAS: Amila
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAmilaAdlam
#. FACE: Angry
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Amila: You. You shall be my second. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 010655C5
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_03_QuestIntro
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013409"
msgid "I accept. I, in fact, look forward to it."
msgstr "받아들일게. 오히려, 아주 기대가 되네."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: What? Why me?
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What? Why me? &&& Amila: Why not you? You seem capable and trustworthy. &&& Danika: The true answer is because Amila has no one, family or otherwise, willing to be his second. He has burned every bridge there is to burn. |He will have to resort to picking someone off the street regardless, so it may as well be you. 
#. ALIAS: Borhal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMBorhalAdlam
#. FACE: Serious
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Amila: Okay, I'll need someone to show me the ropes though. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03
#. TOPIC: 010655B8
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_03_QuestIntro
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013408"
msgid "I do not want to wait any longer than necessary. If you agree to this, you will allow us to come to an immediate resolution. I will pay you handsomely for that."
msgstr ""
"쓸데없이 더 기다리고 싶진 않네. 자네가 동의만 해주면, 즉시 우리 문제의 해법을 실행할 수 있을 걸세. 그렇게 해 준다면 후하게 보상을 "
"쳐주지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry
#. VOICE TYPE: RobotModelAGeneric
#. FACE: Angry
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVGenericRobotModelA
#. TOPIC: 0110AE9E
#. INFO GROUP: FormID 0110AEA3
#. TYPE: Combat
#. SUBTYPE: Taunt
msgctxt "013407"
msgid "House Va'ruun shall triumph!"
msgstr "바룬 가문은 승리할 것이다!"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Friendly / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: SherineDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSherineDubas
#. FACE: Friendly
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D2
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLBuilt
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013406"
msgid "In many ways, I suppose my parents were my heroes as a child."
msgstr "여러모로, 어렸을 때 부모님은 저의 영웅이었던 것 같아요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Somber, heavy heart / Somber / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: How are you coping with the recent calamity in the city?
#. ALIAS: SherineDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSherineDubas
#. FACE: Somber
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D0
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLCalamity
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013405"
msgid "By the grace of the Serpent, we were spared."
msgstr "위대한 뱀 님의 은혜 덕분에, 저희는 환난을 면했어요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: SherineDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSherineDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D0
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLCalamity
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013404"
msgid "Even so, my dreams have been filled with darkness and dread every night."
msgstr "그렇지만, 매일 밤 계속 어둠과 두려움이 가득한 꿈을 꿔요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Trying to be strong, reassuring yourself / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: SherineDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSherineDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D0
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLCalamity
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013403"
msgid "I believe the Great Serpent is testing us, and we must rise to the challenge."
msgstr "저는 위대한 뱀께서 우리를 시험하고 계신 거라 믿어요. 그리고 우리는 그 시련에 맞서 일어나야 해요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Resolved / Confident / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: SherineDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSherineDubas
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D0
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLCalamity
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013402"
msgid "We must be strong and resourceful and prove our devotion beyond all doubt."
msgstr "우리는 강해지고, 지혜로워져야 하며, 의심의 여지가 없게끔 우리의 헌신을 증명해야 해요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: SherineDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSherineDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D0
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLCalamity
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013401"
msgid "Only then will we prove ourselves worthy."
msgstr "그래야만 우리가 가치 있다는 것을 증명할 수 있을 테니까요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker: 
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110ED05
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_070_CouncilMeetings_Scene07
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013400"
msgid "I would like to bring up the topic of our \"acting\" Speaker."
msgstr "대변자 '직무 대행' 문제를 논의하고자 하오."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: Understood. Let us table the matter and proceed to the next item on the agenda.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B189
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_070_CouncilMeetings_Scene07
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133FF"
msgid "Of course. We will table the matter for now. And on that note, it appears we are out of time."
msgstr "물론이지요. 이 문제는 일단 보류하겠습니다. 그러고 보니, 시간이 다 된 것 같군요."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: Which means we have no timetable for such talks to even begin. |We also do not have a process for electing a new Speaker when the time comes. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: It's unfortunate Anasko had no children. It would make the succession much more simple. &&& Kadic_Djimal: Or difficult, if the current regime continues to grip the seat so tightly. &&& Speaker: Do not question my motives, Mediary. I sit on this seat to serve House Va'ruun and the city of Dazra.|And I will continue to serve as Speaker until I alone deem it necessary to step down.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Of course. We will table the matter for now. And on that note, it appears we are out of time.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B18A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_070_CouncilMeetings_Scene07
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133FE"
msgid "Understood. Let us table the matter and proceed to the next item on the agenda."
msgstr "알겠습니다. 이 안건은 보류하고 다음 안건으로 넘어가지요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker:  &&& Kadic_Djimal: I would like to bring up the topic of our "acting" Speaker.|When this role was chosen, it was meant to be a temporary position. But as each day passes, it feels more and more permanent. &&& Speaker: Unfortunately the city is in no condition for such a blanket transfer of power.|I will continue to act as Speaker until things stabilize.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Defiant
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B188
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_070_CouncilMeetings_Scene07
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133FD"
msgid "Which means we have no timetable for such talks to even begin."
msgstr "그 말은 곧 그런 주제를 논의조차 하지 않을 거라는 뜻이군요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Kadic_Djimal: I would like to bring up the topic of our "acting" Speaker.|When this role was chosen, it was meant to be a temporary position. But as each day passes, it feels more and more permanent.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFRazmaKadic
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B187
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_070_CouncilMeetings_Scene07
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133FB"
msgid "Unfortunately the city is in no condition for such a blanket transfer of power."
msgstr "안타깝지만 우리 도시는 그렇게 전면적인 권력 이양을 할 여건이 안 돼."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker: Unfortunately the city is in no condition for such a blanket transfer of power.|I will continue to act as Speaker until things stabilize. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Which means we have no timetable for such talks to even begin. |We also do not have a process for electing a new Speaker when the time comes. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: It's unfortunate Anasko had no children. It would make the succession much more simple. &&& Kadic_Djimal: Or difficult, if the current regime continues to grip the seat so tightly.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMViktorVethaal
#. FACE: Defiant
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B185
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_070_CouncilMeetings_Scene07
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133F8"
msgid "Do not question my motives, Mediary. I sit on this seat to serve House Va'ruun and the city of Dazra."
msgstr "내 동기를 의심하지 마라, 중개자. 나는 바룬 가문과 다즈라를 위해서 이 자리에 앉아 있단 말이다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker: Unfortunately the city is in no condition for such a blanket transfer of power.|I will continue to act as Speaker until things stabilize. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Which means we have no timetable for such talks to even begin. |We also do not have a process for electing a new Speaker when the time comes. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: It's unfortunate Anasko had no children. It would make the succession much more simple. &&& Kadic_Djimal: Or difficult, if the current regime continues to grip the seat so tightly.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFRazmaKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B185
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_070_CouncilMeetings_Scene07
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133F7"
msgid "I will remind the entire Council that I was cast into this position out of necessity. That need still exists."
msgstr "대의회 전체에 상기키시고 싶군. 이 직책은 필요해서 앉게 된 자리이고, 아직도 그 필요성이 남아 있다고 말이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker: Unfortunately the city is in no condition for such a blanket transfer of power.|I will continue to act as Speaker until things stabilize. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Which means we have no timetable for such talks to even begin. |We also do not have a process for electing a new Speaker when the time comes. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: It's unfortunate Anasko had no children. It would make the succession much more simple. &&& Kadic_Djimal: Or difficult, if the current regime continues to grip the seat so tightly.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMHasmakDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B185
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_070_CouncilMeetings_Scene07
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133F6"
msgid "I understand how it looks, but now is not the time dallying over minor political squabbles."
msgstr "어떻게 보이는지는 내 이해하네만, 지금은 사소한 정치 싸움에 매달릴 때가 아닐세."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker:  &&& Kadic_Djimal: I'd like to bring up the subject of immigration.|As you all know, we have agents all across the Settled Systems, which include people from outside Va'ruun'kai.|It's my belief that many of these people would be willing to serve House Va'ruun and become Promised.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: I strongly disagree. Our city is in a state of chaos, and you would bring our enemies to our front door? No, I cannot abide.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B182
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133F3"
msgid "There is precedence, given recent events, and additional hands are very much needed."
msgstr "최근에 벌어진 일을 감안하면 이미 전례도 있고, 추가 인력이 절실한 상황이지요."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: Moving on. Let us proceed to the next item on the agenda.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B52
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133F2"
msgid "Not to interrupt, but it appears we are out of time."
msgstr "방해하려는 건 아닙니다만, 시간이 다 된 것 같군요."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: Nor should they be asked to. The blame should fall on no single party.|We may also want to safeguard the former Speaker's reputation, considering he was the voice of the Great Serpent. &&& Kadic_Djimal: I disagree. We will want to remove the mystique of Jinan's line. The acting Speaker being of a different House is bound to cause fissures. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: The mystique exists for a reason. Blaming the grandson of Jinan Va'ruun, regardless of its veracity, is not a path I'd care to walk. &&& Speaker: No, we present the truth. The Great Serpent Himself passed judgment on Anasko Va'ruun and severed his line. |To question my authority as acting Speaker is to question His will, and those who doubt will be dealt with in full display of the populace.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Not to interrupt, but it appears we are out of time.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B15D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133F1"
msgid "Understood. Let us proceed to the next item on the agenda."
msgstr "알겠습니다. 다음 안건으로 넘어가지요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker: 
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: There has been talk brewing of the experiment itself. Naturally the Ministry of State will correct the error of their ways.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B15E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133F0"
msgid "We should have a discussion about any potential leaks regarding the nature of the cataclysm."
msgstr "이번 대재난의 본질에 대한 정보가 새어나갈 가능성에 대해서 논의해야 합니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker:  &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: We should have a discussion about any potential leaks regarding the nature of the cataclysm. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: There has been talk brewing of the experiment itself. Naturally the Ministry of State will correct the error of their ways.
#. ALIAS: Kadic_Djimal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDjimalKadic
#. FACE: Defiant
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B15B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133EF"
msgid "That's fine, but what's the official story? Blaming the Zealots is convenient, but also difficult to explain."
msgstr "그렇다 치고, 공식 발표는 어떻게 하죠? 광신도 탓으로 돌리면 편리하긴 하지만, 설명하기도 어려운데요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. ALIAS: Kadic_Djimal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDjimalKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Nor should they be asked to. The blame should fall on no single party.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B15B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133EE"
msgid "I doubt the Ministry of State will want such an embarassment to fall on their House."
msgstr "국무성도 본인들 가문이 망신당할 일은 원하지 않을 텐데 말이죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker:  &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: We should have a discussion about any potential leaks regarding the nature of the cataclysm.
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Kadic_Djimal: That's fine, but what's the official story? Blaming the Zealots is convenient, but also difficult to explain.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B15A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133ED"
msgid "There has been talk brewing of the experiment itself. Naturally the Ministry of State will correct the error of their ways."
msgstr "실험 자체에 대한 이야기가 나오고 있더군. 당연히 국무성에서 그런 잘못된 태도를 바로잡을 것이오."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Kadic_Djimal: That's fine, but what's the official story? Blaming the Zealots is convenient, but also difficult to explain.|I doubt the Ministry of State will want such an embarassment to fall on their House. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Nor should they be asked to. The blame should fall on no single party.|We may also want to safeguard the former Speaker's reputation, considering he was the voice of the Great Serpent.
#. ALIAS: Kadic_Djimal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDjimalKadic
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: The mystique exists for a reason. Blaming the grandson of Jinan Va'ruun, regardless of its veracity, is not a path I'd care to walk.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B157
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133EC"
msgid "I disagree. We will want to remove the mystique of Jinan's line. The acting Speaker being of a different House is bound to cause fissures."
msgstr "난 반대에요. 지난 님의 혈통에 대한 신비주의를 지워야 해요. 다른 가문에서 대변자 직무 대행을 맡으면 균열이 생길 거라고요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: We should have a discussion about any potential leaks regarding the nature of the cataclysm. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: There has been talk brewing of the experiment itself. Naturally the Ministry of State will correct the error of their ways. &&& Kadic_Djimal: That's fine, but what's the official story? Blaming the Zealots is convenient, but also difficult to explain.|I doubt the Ministry of State will want such an embarassment to fall on their House.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B159
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133EB"
msgid "Nor should they be asked to. The blame should fall on no single party."
msgstr "그런 요구를 해서도 안 되지요. 한쪽에만 책임을 전가하면 안 됩니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Vethaal_Lovek
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Kadic_Djimal: I disagree. We will want to remove the mystique of Jinan's line. The acting Speaker being of a different House is bound to cause fissures.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B159
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133EA"
msgid "We may also want to safeguard the former Speaker's reputation, considering he was the voice of the Great Serpent."
msgstr "그리고 전임 대변자님의 평판을 보호해야 할 겁니다. 그분께서 곧 위대한 뱀의 목소리였다는 점을 고려하면 말이지요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Nor should they be asked to. The blame should fall on no single party.|We may also want to safeguard the former Speaker's reputation, considering he was the voice of the Great Serpent. &&& Kadic_Djimal: I disagree. We will want to remove the mystique of Jinan's line. The acting Speaker being of a different House is bound to cause fissures. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: The mystique exists for a reason. Blaming the grandson of Jinan Va'ruun, regardless of its veracity, is not a path I'd care to walk.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMViktorVethaal
#. FACE: Defiant
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B158
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133E9"
msgid "No, we present the truth. The Great Serpent Himself passed judgment on Anasko Va'ruun and severed his line."
msgstr "아니. 우리는 진실을 발표할 것이다. 위대한 뱀께서 아나스코 바룬을 심판하시고 그 혈통을 끊으셨다고 말이다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Nor should they be asked to. The blame should fall on no single party.|We may also want to safeguard the former Speaker's reputation, considering he was the voice of the Great Serpent. &&& Kadic_Djimal: I disagree. We will want to remove the mystique of Jinan's line. The acting Speaker being of a different House is bound to cause fissures. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: The mystique exists for a reason. Blaming the grandson of Jinan Va'ruun, regardless of its veracity, is not a path I'd care to walk.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFRazmaKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Understood. Let us proceed to the next item on the agenda.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B158
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133E8"
msgid "We should tell the people the truth. If Anasko's reputation cannot survive that, then it is the Great Serpent's will. All Must Serve."
msgstr "신민들에게 진실을 말해야 해. 아나스코 님의 평판을 지키지 못한다면, 그것도 위대한 뱀의 뜻이겠지. 모두가 섬겨야 한다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Nor should they be asked to. The blame should fall on no single party.|We may also want to safeguard the former Speaker's reputation, considering he was the voice of the Great Serpent. &&& Kadic_Djimal: I disagree. We will want to remove the mystique of Jinan's line. The acting Speaker being of a different House is bound to cause fissures. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: The mystique exists for a reason. Blaming the grandson of Jinan Va'ruun, regardless of its veracity, is not a path I'd care to walk.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMHasmakDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Understood. Let us proceed to the next item on the agenda.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B158
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133E7"
msgid "This discussion will need to be tabled. There are far too many variables that I will need to consider."
msgstr "이 논의는 나중으로 미뤄야 할 것 같네. 내가 고려해야 할 변수가 너무 많구먼."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Question
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Vethaal_Lovek: There has been talk brewing of the experiment itself. Naturally the Ministry of State will correct the error of their ways. &&& Kadic_Djimal: That's fine, but what's the official story? Blaming the Zealots is convenient, but also difficult to explain.|I doubt the Ministry of State will want such an embarassment to fall on their House. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Nor should they be asked to. The blame should fall on no single party.|We may also want to safeguard the former Speaker's reputation, considering he was the voice of the Great Serpent. &&& Kadic_Djimal: I disagree. We will want to remove the mystique of Jinan's line. The acting Speaker being of a different House is bound to cause fissures.
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Question
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Speaker: No, we present the truth. The Great Serpent Himself passed judgment on Anasko Va'ruun and severed his line. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110B156
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_060_CouncilMeetings_Scene06
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133E6"
msgid "The mystique exists for a reason. Blaming the grandson of Jinan Va'ruun, regardless of its veracity, is not a path I'd care to walk."
msgstr "신비주의는 이유가 있어서 있는 거요. 진실 여부를 떠나서 지난 바룬 님의 손자를 비난하는 건 내가 걷고자 하는 길이 아니오."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Speaker, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. ALIAS: Kadic_Djimal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDjimalKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133E5"
msgid "As you all know, we have agents all across the Settled Systems, which include people from outside Va'ruun'kai."
msgstr "다들 아시다시피, 우리는 개척 성계 전역에 요원들을 두고 있어요. 그 중에는 바룬카이 외부 출신도 있죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident / to Speaker, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. ALIAS: Kadic_Djimal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDjimalKadic
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: There is precedence, given recent events, and additional hands are very much needed.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133E4"
msgid "It's my belief that many of these people would be willing to serve House Va'ruun and become Promised."
msgstr "저는 외부 출신 중에 바룬 가문을 섬기고 약속받은 자가 되려 하는 사람들이 많을 거라고 생각해요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. ALIAS: Kadic_Djimal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDjimalKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: House Veth'aal will do its duty, as it always has.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B47
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133E3"
msgid "Unless you doubt the Ministry of State's capability to do so?"
msgstr "아니면, 국무성의 능력을 의심하는 건가요?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMViktorVethaal
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Understood. Let us then move on to the next item on the agenda.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B44
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133E2"
msgid "This \"proposal\" flies in the face of that edict. I will not consider it."
msgstr "이 '제안'은 그 명령에 정면으로 위배되는 것이야. 고려하지 않겠다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMHasmakDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Understood. Let us then move on to the next item on the agenda.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B44
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133E1"
msgid "But I will have to consider this matter further before we proceed."
msgstr "그래도 이 문제는 계속 논의하기 전에 좀 더 생각해 봐야겠구먼."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Inaza: Have you reconsidered my request?
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Serious
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D70E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133E0"
msgid "I have seen visions of Anasko, searching for one bold enough to enter the heart of the vortex."
msgstr "내가 아나스코 님의 환영을 봤다. 볼텍스의 심장부에 들어갈 정도로 용감한 이를 찾고 계셨어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Inaza:  &&& Inaza: Have you reconsidered my request? &&& Inaza: I have seen visions of Anasko, searching for one bold enough to enter the heart of the vortex.|And now that you are here, I know your arrival was no accident. But rather, providence.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Well put. The Great Serpent's works are imperceptible, even to a Herald like myself.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D70D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133DF"
msgid "Indeed. Much of our lives are governed by forces we do not understand."
msgstr "맞아요. 우리 인생의 많은 부분은 우리가 이해하지 못하는 힘에 끌려 다니죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Indeed. Much of our lives are governed by forces we do not understand.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Indeed. Much of our lives are governed by forces we do not understand.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Serious
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Inaza: But rest assured, all will be revealed when you journey north. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D70C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133DE"
msgid "Well put. The Great Serpent's works are imperceptible, even to a Herald like myself."
msgstr "맞는 말이다. 위대한 뱀의 행하심은 나 같은 전령조차도 알아챌 수 없는 법이니."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Inaza:  &&& Inaza: Have you reconsidered my request? &&& Inaza: I have seen visions of Anasko, searching for one bold enough to enter the heart of the vortex.|And now that you are here, I know your arrival was no accident. But rather, providence.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: You cast doubt on my words. It's to be expected.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D70B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133DD"
msgid "Anything can seem like providence to the unenlightened."
msgstr "계몽되지 않은 사람에게는 뭐든지 섭리로 보일 수 있어요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Anything can seem like providence to the unenlightened.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Anything can seem like providence to the unenlightened.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Inaza: But rest assured, all will be revealed when you journey north. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D70A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133DC"
msgid "You cast doubt on my words. It's to be expected."
msgstr "내 말을 의심하는구나. 그럴 것 같았다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Inaza:  &&& Inaza: Have you reconsidered my request? &&& Inaza: I have seen visions of Anasko, searching for one bold enough to enter the heart of the vortex.|And now that you are here, I know your arrival was no accident. But rather, providence.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Worry not. Understanding is not given to those who lack the Herald's eye.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D709
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133DB"
msgid "I don't even know what that means."
msgstr "전 그게 무슨 뜻인지도 모르겠는데요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: I don't even know what that means.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I don't even know what that means.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Inaza: But rest assured, all will be revealed when you journey north. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D708
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133DA"
msgid "Worry not. Understanding is not given to those who lack the Herald's eye."
msgstr "걱정 말거라. 이해는 전령의 시야가 부족한 이들에게 주어진 것이 아니니."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Inaza:  &&& Inaza: Have you reconsidered my request? &&& Inaza: I have seen visions of Anasko, searching for one bold enough to enter the heart of the vortex.|And now that you are here, I know your arrival was no accident. But rather, providence.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: And yet you crossed paths with the Oracle, and found our city hidden amongst the stars.  
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D707
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133D9"
msgid "Your city was in trouble and I came here to help. There's nothing else to it."
msgstr "이 도시가 위험에 처했고 제가 도와주러 왔죠. 단지 그뿐이에요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Your city was in trouble and I came here to help. There's nothing else to it.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Your city was in trouble and I came here to help. There's nothing else to it.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D706
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133D8"
msgid "And yet you crossed paths with the Oracle, and found our city hidden amongst the stars."
msgstr "허나 그대는 오라클과 함께 길을 건너 별들 사이에 숨겨진 우리 도시를 찾아내었지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confused / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Confused
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D704
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133D6"
msgid "And while my readings do not show any anomalous activity, I admit there's a lot of interference."
msgstr "그리고 내 측정 결과에는 이상 역장 활동이 잡히지 않지만, 간섭 요인이 많다는 건 인정하겠어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Inaza: You cast doubt on my words. It's to be expected.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D705
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133D5"
msgid "But rest assured, all will be revealed when you journey north."
msgstr "어쨌든 내 장담컨대, 북쪽으로 가면 모든 것이 드러날 것이다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: That sounds ominous if true. &&& ...  &&& Inaza: In the second future, I saw you make contact with Anasko, entering a cave through a formless wall. &&& Inaza: At its terminus was a gate; a path into the realm where our Speaker resides.|You stepped into this void, and in that moment something changed. The false future, rewritten. &&& Ekris: Hm... roughly speaking, it could be that entering the vortex directly would allow you to speak with him.|And while my readings do not show any anomalous activity, I admit there's a lot of interference.|Still, that only emphasizes the potential danger involved here. I cannot approve of such an excursion on the MINUTE chance Anasko is present.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I am no heretic. But to risk so much on a vision... it is a leap of faith I cannot condone.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D703
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133D4"
msgid "You just need to have a little faith."
msgstr "믿음을 좀 가져보시지 그래요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: You just need to have a little faith.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: You just need to have a little faith.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D702
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133D3"
msgid "I am no heretic. But to risk so much on a vision... it is a leap of faith I cannot condone."
msgstr "난 이단자가 아니야. 하지만 환영 때문에 그렇게 큰 위험을 감수하라니... 그런 무모한 짓은 용납 못 해."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: You just need to have a little faith.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Irritated
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Inaza: You may not realize it now, dear brother, but our goals are one and the same.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D702
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133D2"
msgid "I will not stand in your way, however, as Inaza has stood in ours."
msgstr "그래도 자넬 굳이 막지는 않겠네. 이나자 누님하곤 다르게 말이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: That sounds ominous if true. &&& ...  &&& Inaza: In the second future, I saw you make contact with Anasko, entering a cave through a formless wall. &&& Inaza: At its terminus was a gate; a path into the realm where our Speaker resides.|You stepped into this void, and in that moment something changed. The false future, rewritten. &&& Ekris: Hm... roughly speaking, it could be that entering the vortex directly would allow you to speak with him.|And while my readings do not show any anomalous activity, I admit there's a lot of interference.|Still, that only emphasizes the potential danger involved here. I cannot approve of such an excursion on the MINUTE chance Anasko is present.
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I've said as much myself, but my sister persists. It may save us more time to inspect the cave than to continue these arguments.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D701
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133D1"
msgid "Agreed. I'm not sure this is worth investigating."
msgstr "동감이에요. 조사해 볼 가치가 있을지 잘 모르겠네요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Apologetic / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Agreed. I'm not sure this is worth investigating.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Agreed. I'm not sure this is worth investigating.
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Apologetic
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Inaza: You may not realize it now, dear brother, but our goals are one and the same.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D700
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133D0"
msgid "I've said as much myself, but my sister persists. It may save us more time to inspect the cave than to continue these arguments."
msgstr "나도 그렇게 말했는데, 누님이 고집을 부리시네. 계속 말싸움하느니 그 동굴을 살펴보는 게 시간이 더 절약될 것 같아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: You just need to have a little faith. &&& Ekris: I am no heretic. But to risk so much on a vision... it is a leap of faith I cannot condone.|I will not stand in your way, however, as Inaza has stood in ours. &&& Inaza: You may not realize it now, dear brother, but our goals are one and the same.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Then you must embark to the northern edge of the crater. You will find an entrance there, one that has no form.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D6FB
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133CF"
msgid "If you point me to the cave, I can find him."
msgstr "그 동굴 위치를 알려주시면 찾아 보죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: That sounds ominous if true. &&& ...  &&& Inaza: In the second future, I saw you make contact with Anasko, entering a cave through a formless wall. &&& Inaza: At its terminus was a gate; a path into the realm where our Speaker resides.|You stepped into this void, and in that moment something changed. The false future, rewritten. &&& Ekris: Hm... roughly speaking, it could be that entering the vortex directly would allow you to speak with him.|And while my readings do not show any anomalous activity, I admit there's a lot of interference.|Still, that only emphasizes the potential danger involved here. I cannot approve of such an excursion on the MINUTE chance Anasko is present.
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: The closer one ventures to the heart of the anomaly, the closer they are to the phantoms and horrors that lie within.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D6FF
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133CE"
msgid "What kind of danger?"
msgstr "어떤 위험이 있죠?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: What kind of danger?
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What kind of danger?
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D6FE
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133CD"
msgid "The closer one ventures to the heart of the anomaly, the closer they are to the phantoms and horrors that lie within."
msgstr "이상 역장의 중심부에 가까이 가면 갈수록, 그 안에 있는 유령과 호러와도 가까워지는 셈이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concentrating / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: What kind of danger?
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Concentrating
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Ekris: You just need to have a little faith.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D6FE
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133CC"
msgid "Moreover, if this \"cave\" was cut open by the calamity itself, then it is an unnatural formation and highly unstable."
msgstr "게다가 만약 그 '동굴'이 대재난 때문에 열린 거라면, 분명 부자연스럽고 굉장히 불안정한 지형이겠지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Apologetic / to Ekris
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: You just need to have a little faith. &&& Ekris: I am no heretic. But to risk so much on a vision... it is a leap of faith I cannot condone.|I will not stand in your way, however, as Inaza has stood in ours.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Apologetic
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: If you point me to the cave, I can find him.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D6FC
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133CB"
msgid "You may not realize it now, dear brother, but our goals are one and the same."
msgstr "사랑하는 동생아. 지금은 잘 모르겠지만, 우리 목표는 서로 같단다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Can you tell me more about this location?
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Can you tell me more about this location?
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D6F7
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133CA"
msgid "It was a winding cave, scattered with walls of dark energy. At the end, a rip in the fabric of reality."
msgstr "어두운 에너지로 된 벽이 흩어져 있는 구불구불한 동굴이었다. 그 끝에는 현실의 구조가 찢어져 있었지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Can you tell me more about this location?
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D6F7
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133C9"
msgid "In my vision, I saw you step forward, slowly, following the sound of Anasko's voice. I could hear him calling to you in the distance."
msgstr ""
"환영 속에서, 그대가 아나스코 님의 목소리를 따라 천천히 나아가는 모습을 보았다. 저 멀리서 그분이 그대를 부르는 소리도 들렸어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Can you tell me more about this location?
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Concerned
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Inaza: If you point me to the cave, I can find him.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D6F7
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133C8"
msgid "His words were jumbled, but as you drew closer, they started to assemble. I was thrust out of the vision before I could see the end."
msgstr "그분의 말은 혼란스러웠지만, 가까이 다가가자 명확해졌단다. 마지막 장면을 보기 전에 환영을 놓치고 말았지만 말이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Inaza: And they will be made husks in the end, just as Jinan foretold.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Ekris: *Sigh*, fine. I feel like I've lived this argument a thousand times, and the only way to move past it is to concede to its nonsense.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110B5FA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_020_QuestStart
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133C7"
msgid "But the proof is not in our words. It is in the vision. Anasko's presence still persists in this world, and he seeks our aid."
msgstr "어쨌든 말이 증거가 될 수는 없지. 증거는 바로 환영이란다. 아나스코 님의 존재가 여전히 이 세상에 남아 도움을 구하고 있어."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Inaza: Then you must embark to the northern edge of the crater. You will find an entrance there, one that has no form.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D6F9
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133C6"
msgid "Step through it, find Anasko, and complete the vision. Only then will his voice be heard."
msgstr "입구를 통과해 아나스코 님을 찾고 환영을 완성하거라. 그래야만 그분의 목소리가 들릴 것이다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: You just need to have a little faith. &&& Ekris: I am no heretic. But to risk so much on a vision... it is a leap of faith I cannot condone.|I will not stand in your way, however, as Inaza has stood in ours. &&& Inaza: You may not realize it now, dear brother, but our goals are one and the same.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: It was a winding cave, scattered with walls of dark energy. At the end, a rip in the fabric of reality.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D6F8
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133C5"
msgid "Can you tell me more about this location?"
msgstr "그 장소에 대해서 자세히 말해줄 수 있을까요?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Ekris: With all due respect to your craft, dear sister, now is not the time for incense and ash leaves. 
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Inaza: On the contrary, brother, I see it for what it truly is.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110B5F9
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_000_IntroScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133C4"
msgid "Or do you not see the depth of the crater before you."
msgstr "이 앞에 있는 깊은 구덩이가 안 보이시우?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious / to InazaHeadtrack
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Inaza: On the contrary, brother, I see it for what it truly is.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Serious
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Ekris: Enough with the proselytizing.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110B5F8
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_000_IntroScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133C3"
msgid "And if we ignore this vision, Anasko will be lost to us forever."
msgstr "그리고 그 환영을 무시하면, 우린 아나스코 님을 영원히 잃게 될 게다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: If you point me to the cave, I can find him.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: If you point me to the cave, I can find him.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Inaza: Step through it, find Anasko, and complete the vision. Only then will his voice be heard. 
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110D6FA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_030_InazaGreet
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133C2"
msgid "Then you must embark to the northern edge of the crater. You will find an entrance there, one that has no form."
msgstr "그렇다면 구덩이 북쪽 가장자리로 향해야 한다. 그곳에서 형체가 없는 입구를 찾을 수 있을 것이다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Our works will succeed because they are backed by science. Not because of some religious mumbo jumbo.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Our works will succeed because they are backed by science. Not because of some religious mumbo jumbo.
#. ALIAS: Inaza
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Angry
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Inaza: But the proof is not in our words. It is in the vision. Anasko's presence still persists in this world, and he seeks our aid.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110AFA0
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_020_QuestStart
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133C1"
msgid "I will forgive you for not knowing our customs, but I will not tolerate such blasphemy."
msgstr "우리 관습을 모르는 거야 용서하겠지만, 그런 신성 모독은 용납할 수 없다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Indeed. The Shrouding obscures the way forward for those who lack faith.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Indeed. The Shrouding obscures the way forward for those who lack faith.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFInazaKaisir
#. FACE: Serious
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Inaza: But the proof is not in our words. It is in the vision. Anasko's presence still persists in this world, and he seeks our aid.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQIN
#. TOPIC: 0110AF9C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQIN_020_QuestStart
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133C0"
msgid "And they will be made husks in the end, just as Jinan foretold."
msgstr "그리고 지난 님께서 예언하신 대로 허물이 되어 버리겠지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated / to Amila
#. ALIAS: Amila
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAmilaAdlam
#. FACE: Irritated
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Borhal: No, no. I... I was foolish, Amila. The duel is off, and it should have never happened to begin with.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FE
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133BE"
msgid "What do you want, brother? Is it time to resume our duel?"
msgstr "뭘 원하는 거지, 형? 이제 서로 결투를 재개할 때가 됐나?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Apologetic / to Amila
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Amila: What do you want, brother? Is it time to resume our duel?
#. ALIAS: Borhal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMBorhalAdlam
#. FACE: Apologetic
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FD
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133BD"
msgid "No, no. I... I was foolish, Amila. The duel is off, and it should have never happened to begin with."
msgstr "아니, 아니란다. 내... 내가 어리석었어, 동생아. 결투는 끝났고, 처음부터 일어나서는 안 되는 일이었다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Apologetic / to Amila
#. ALIAS: Borhal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMBorhalAdlam
#. FACE: Apologetic
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FD
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133BC"
msgid "The truth is that, when the duel was sabotaged, I had never felt so relieved in my life."
msgstr "솔직히, 결투에 방해 요소가 생겼을 때 내 인생에서 그렇게 안도감을 느낀 적이 없었어..."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Apologetic / to Amila
#. ALIAS: Borhal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMBorhalAdlam
#. FACE: Apologetic
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FD
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133BB"
msgid "I do not want to kill you, Amila. I am ashamed to have ever challenged you. I am sorry."
msgstr "널 죽이고 싶지 않아, 아밀라. 결투를 신청해서 정말 수치스럽구나. 미안하다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Apologetic / to Amila
#. ALIAS: Borhal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMBorhalAdlam
#. FACE: Apologetic
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Amila: I...
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FD
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133BA"
msgid "I understand if you never want to speak with me again. I am disgusted in myself."
msgstr "다신 나와 얘기하고 싶지 않다면 이해해 주겠다. 나도 내 자신이 역겹구나."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Surprised / to Borhal
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Amila: What do you want, brother? Is it time to resume our duel? &&& Borhal: No, no. I... I was foolish, Amila. The duel is off, and it should have never happened to begin with.|The truth is that, when the duel was sabotaged, I had never felt so relieved in my life.|I do not want to kill you, Amila. I am ashamed to have ever challenged you. I am sorry.|I understand if you never want to speak with me again. I am disgusted in myself.
#. ALIAS: Amila
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAmilaAdlam
#. FACE: Surprised
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FC
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133B9"
msgid "I..."
msgstr "난..."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Borhal
#. ALIAS: Amila
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAmilaAdlam
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Borhal: No jokes, Amila, please. I just want you to know that I am sorry.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FC
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133B8"
msgid "Oh, come now, brother. I deserved it all. You have shown me nothing but patience for years, but even the patience of a saint can run out."
msgstr ""
"아니야, 형... 난 그 정도는 당해도 쌌어. 몇 년 동안 계속 나를 참고 지켜봤으면서, 성인군자라 해도 인내심이 한계가 있겠지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Apologetic / to Amila
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Borhal: No, no. I... I was foolish, Amila. The duel is off, and it should have never happened to begin with.|The truth is that, when the duel was sabotaged, I had never felt so relieved in my life.|I do not want to kill you, Amila. I am ashamed to have ever challenged you. I am sorry.|I understand if you never want to speak with me again. I am disgusted in myself. &&& Amila: I...|Oh, come now, brother. I deserved it all. You have shown me nothing but patience for years, but even the patience of a saint can run out.
#. ALIAS: Borhal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMBorhalAdlam
#. FACE: Apologetic
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Amila: I am, too.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FB
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133B7"
msgid "No jokes, Amila, please. I just want you to know that I am sorry."
msgstr "농담이 아니다, 아밀라. 내가 미안하단 사실을 알려 주고 싶었을 뿐이다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Grateful / to Borhal
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Amila: I...|Oh, come now, brother. I deserved it all. You have shown me nothing but patience for years, but even the patience of a saint can run out. &&& Borhal: No jokes, Amila, please. I just want you to know that I am sorry.
#. ALIAS: Amila
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAmilaAdlam
#. FACE: Grateful
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133B6"
msgid "I am, too."
msgstr "나도 그래."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Borhal
#. ALIAS: Amila
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAmilaAdlam
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133B5"
msgid "I will... I will try to be better. I cannot make any promises. All I can say is that I will try."
msgstr "앞으로... 더 나은 사람이 될게. 약속은 못하지만. 시도는 해 보겠다고 말할 수 있어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Borhal
#. ALIAS: Amila
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAmilaAdlam
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Borhal: It is all right Amila. One thing at a time.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7FA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133B4"
msgid "I want to make things right with you, with everyone. But, I just do not know where to start."
msgstr "형이랑, 모두와 관계를 바로잡고 싶어. 하지만, 어디서 시작해야 할지 모르겠어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Amila
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Borhal: No jokes, Amila, please. I just want you to know that I am sorry. &&& Amila: I am, too.|I will... I will try to be better. I cannot make any promises. All I can say is that I will try.|I want to make things right with you, with everyone. But, I just do not know where to start.
#. ALIAS: Borhal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMBorhalAdlam
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene
#. TOPIC: 0110B7F9
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS03_PostQuestScene_01
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133B3"
msgid "It is all right Amila. One thing at a time."
msgstr "다 괜찮아. 아밀라. 한 번에 하나씩 하면 돼."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMViktorVethaal
#. FACE: Serious
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ04
#. TOPIC: 01104110
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_MQ04_7000_ViktorHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "0133B2"
msgid "You have the codes. See to their delivery."
msgstr "전력망 접속 코드 줬잖나. 코드를 전달했는지 확인하도록."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Irritated / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Were you and Vaeric close?
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Were you and Vaeric close?
#. ALIAS: Smuggler
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMTaneSalavea
#. FACE: Irritated
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Smuggler: I couldn't have done it without your help.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_TaneSalavea
#. TOPIC: 01003A32
#. SCENE: DLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Smuggler_RecruitScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133A4"
msgid "Nah, not close. But I get why he wanted out. Va'ruun life ain't easy. It's a kick in the teeth on its best days."
msgstr ""
"아니, 썩 친하진 않았지. 다만 왜 떠나길 바랐는지 알겠어. 바룬의 삶은 쉽지 않아. 좋을 때도 얼굴에 발차기가 날아오는 것 같지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Smuggler: Long time no see. You change your mind about the crew thing? Might be a good fit.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: So that's your play, huh, gassing me up. Eh, I don't care enough to stop you.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_TaneSalavea
#. TOPIC: 01003A37
#. SCENE: DLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Smuggler_RecruitScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133A3"
msgid "I'm still grateful for your help in tracking him down."
msgstr "아직도 그 친구를 추적하는 데 도와줘서 참 고마운 심정이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Smuggler: Long time no see. You change your mind about the crew thing? Might be a good fit.
#. ALIAS: Smuggler
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Yeah, yeah, I know. You don't have to rub it in though. No one likes a show off.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_TaneSalavea
#. TOPIC: 01003A3A
#. SCENE: DLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Smuggler_RecruitScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133A2"
msgid "Just be glad I did what needed to be done, or else Viktor might've come after you."
msgstr "내가 해야 할 일을 했던 것에 기뻐하라고, 아니면 빅토르가 널 잡으러 왔을지 몰라."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Yeah, you have enough problems as it is.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Yeah, you have enough problems as it is.
#. ALIAS: Smuggler
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMTaneSalavea
#. FACE: Concerned
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Smuggler: Anyway, seeing as I don't have a ship, I'm kind of out of a job.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_TaneSalavea
#. TOPIC: 01003A34
#. SCENE: DLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Smuggler_RecruitScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133A1"
msgid "Yeah, but there's problems and then there's PROBLEMS. This was the capital kind."
msgstr "그래, 근데 평범한 문제가 있고 심각한 문제가 있지. 예전 그 일은 심각한 문제였어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: Smuggler
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMTaneSalavea
#. FACE: Serious
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_TaneSalavea
#. TOPIC: 01003A38
#. SCENE: DLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Smuggler_RecruitScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0133A0"
msgid "Hmph. Not sure I should be happy to see you, seeing as how that whole thing with Vaeric went down."
msgstr "흥. 배릭과의 일이 그렇게 된 걸 보면 자네를 보고 기뻐해야 할지 모르겠구먼."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: Smuggler
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMTaneSalavea
#. FACE: Serious
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Smuggler:  Welcome aboard.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_TaneSalavea
#. TOPIC: 01003A38
#. SCENE: DLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Smuggler_RecruitScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01339F"
msgid "Still, that's the way it goes sometimes, and I know better than to piss you off."
msgstr "그래도, 사람 일은 가끔 그런 법이지. 그리고 함부로 널 화나게 하고 싶지 않아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Sahima: It's only a remnant of what it once was. The Scaled Citadel, missing from the horizon, is a constant reminder of that.
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Sahima: To me, cities are like people. They have personalities, moods, and stories.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 0110AAE2
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_Dazra
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01339E"
msgid "And yet, I still feel Dazra offers much to a visitor like yourself."
msgstr "그래도 너 같은 방문자에게 다즈라는 여전히 좋은 볼거리가 될 것 같아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Sahima: But the question must be asked, lest it repeat itself.
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 0110AAD6
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraHouseDivided
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01339D"
msgid "Regardless, I've heard Razma will be enforcing stricter guidelines for new members going forward."
msgstr "어쨌든 라즈마가 이제부터 새 사람을 받아들일 때 더 기준을 엄격하게 할 거라고 들었어."

#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 0110AAD6
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraHouseDivided
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01339C"
msgid "It is necessary, but at the same time, I wonder if we are closing the very door I once used to become a Ka'dic."
msgstr "필요하긴 하지만, 내가 카딕의 일원이 될 수 있었던 그 등용문이 닫히는 것 같아 걱정돼."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Oh-keem. / Somber
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Somber
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Sahima: You mentioned dealing with feelings of insecurity. Have you had time to digest our earlier talk?
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 0110AAD6
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraHouseDivided
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01339B"
msgid "Because I cannot help but see the parallels between myself and Ochim. *Sigh*, time will tell."
msgstr "왜냐하면 나와 오킴 사이의 유사점이 뻔히 보이기 때문이야. *한숨*, 시간이 지나면 알 수 있겠지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Thinking / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: As a member of House Ka'dic, will you have any influence?
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What changes do you see with House Veth'aal?
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Thinking
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 010B2BB9
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraFuture
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01339A"
msgid "I anticipate stricter rules, and less tolerance for Zealots."
msgstr "규칙은 더 엄중해지고, 광신도들에게도 더 가차 없어지겠지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: As a member of House Ka'dic, will you have any influence?
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Concerned
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 010B2BB9
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraFuture
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013399"
msgid "I worry the scales may tip too far, but they need to be tipped, if what happened to me is any indication."
msgstr "지나치게 한쪽에만 유리해질 것 같지만 그렇게 되어야 해. 나한테 벌어진 일을 봐서라도."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Afraid / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: As a member of House Ka'dic, will you have any influence?
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Afraid
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Sahima: I think so. I chose them because they're the best equipped for what's ahead.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 010B2BB9
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraFuture
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013398"
msgid "But I've also heard rumors of a potential curfew. That would be disastrous!"
msgstr "근데 통금까지 생길 수도 있단 얘길 들었어. 그럼 정말 끔찍하겠는데!"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Thinking / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: As a member of House Ka'dic, will you have any influence?
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What changes do you see with House Veth'aal?
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Thinking
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 010B2BB9
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraFuture
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013397"
msgid "Hasmak Dul'kehf is known for being meticulous to a fault. I anticipate there will be more structure."
msgstr "해즈막 둘케프는 심할 정도로 주의가 깊은 사람으로 잘 알려져 있지. 앞으로 더 많은 구조가 생길 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: As a member of House Ka'dic, will you have any influence?
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Concerned
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 010B2BB9
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraFuture
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013396"
msgid "But structure and freedom have a testy relationship. So I am worried that our roles will become more rigid."
msgstr "그러나 구조와 자유의 서로 까다로운 관계 때문에 우리의 역할도 좀 더 경직될 것 같아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Afraid / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: As a member of House Ka'dic, will you have any influence?
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Afraid
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Sahima: I think so. I chose them because they're the best equipped for what's ahead.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 010B2BB9
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraFuture
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
#, fuzzy
msgctxt "013395"
msgid "As a member of your crew, I enjoy having a flexible schedule. I am afraid the citizens will lose that in favor of specializiation."
msgstr "네 승무원의 일원으로서, 나는 유연한 일정을 갖는 것을 좋아해. 신민들이 전문성을 키우려다 그런 것을 잃을까 봐 걱정돼."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What do you think of Dazra's future? &&& Sahima: Heisenberg's principle states that all things have uncertainty, that nothing can be measured with precision. The same is true of the future. &&& Sahima: But I am hopeful that Viktor Veth'aal will serve the role of Speaker with honor and faith.|If nothing else, I won't have to worry about being kidnapped by Zealots on his watch.
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Not that I know of. But perhaps, indirectly.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 010B2BBA
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraFuture
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013394"
msgid "What changes do you see with House Veth'aal?"
msgstr "앞으로 베타알 가문에서 어떤 변화가 있을 것 같아?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What do you think of Dazra's future? &&& Sahima: Heisenberg's principle states that all things have uncertainty, that nothing can be measured with precision. The same is true of the future. &&& Sahima: But I am hopeful that Razma will serve the role of Speaker with honor and faith.|If nothing else, I will have a direct line to her. We sleep in the same house!
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Not that I know of. But perhaps, indirectly.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 010B2BBA
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraFuture
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013393"
msgid "What changes do you see with House Dul'kehf?"
msgstr "둘케프 가문은 이제 어떤 변화를 거칠 것 같아?"

#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I think so. I chose them because they're the best equipped for what's ahead.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 010B2BBB
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraFuture
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013392"
msgid "If nothing else, I will have a direct line to her. We sleep in the same house!"
msgstr "못해도 그 사람에게 직접 소통할 창구가 생기는 거잖아. 서로 같은 집에서 자니까!"

#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I think so. I chose them because they're the best equipped for what's ahead.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 010B2BBB
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraFuture
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013391"
msgid "If nothing else, I won't have to worry about being kidnapped by Zealots on his watch."
msgstr "못해도 그분이 감시하는 동안에는 광신도들에게 납치당할 염려는 안 해도 되겠지."

#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I think so. I chose them because they're the best equipped for what's ahead.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 010B2BBB
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_DazraFuture
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013390"
msgid "If nothing else, things will run on time."
msgstr "아무리 못해도 모든 일이 예정대로 진행되겠지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Somber
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Can I ask you about Dazra?
#. ALIAS: Sahima
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSahimaKadic
#. FACE: Somber
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Sahima: And yet, I still feel Dazra offers much to a visitor like yourself.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_CREW_EliteCrew_SahimaKadic
#. TOPIC: 01038C7C
#. SCENE: SFBGSDLC001_CREW_EliteCrew_Sahima_TopLevel_Dazra
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01338F"
msgid "It's only a remnant of what it once was. The Scaled Citadel, trapped on the horizon, is a constant reminder of that."
msgstr "이젠 옛 과거의 폐허뿐이지. 비늘 성채도 저 너머에 홀로 격리되어 그 재난을 계속 상기시켜 주고 있어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: In House Va'ruun, children come of age when they slaughter their groat and make a dagger from their bones. Vassilis is making an analogy / Apologetic
#. ALIAS: Z03_Vassilis
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVassilisVoyiatzi
#. FACE: Apologetic
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVDazra
#. TOPIC: 010FBEDC
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHVDazra_Vassilis_TL_Profession
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01338E"
msgid "But one cannot serve the House without first carving the dagger."
msgstr "하지만 뼈 단검조차 직접 깎지 못하는 사람은 가문에 봉사할 수도 없죠."

