msgctxt "0132C5"
msgid "Your presence here is unauthorized."
msgstr "귀하가 이곳에 있는 건 허용되지 않았습니다."

#. VOICE TYPE: RobotModelAGeneric
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVGenericRobotModelA
#. TOPIC: 010D246F
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_GenericModelA_Hellos01
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "0132C4"
msgid "It is advisable for all residents to stay calm amidst the current emergency situation."
msgstr "모든 주민들은 현재 위급 상황에 평정을 유지하시길 권고합니다."

#. VOICE TYPE: RobotModelAGeneric
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVGenericRobotModelA
#. TOPIC: 010D246F
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_GenericModelA_Hellos01
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "0132C3"
msgid "We urge everyone to remain composed during this crisis."
msgstr "여러분 모두 이 재난 상황에 침착을 유지하길 바랍니다."

#. VOICE TYPE: RobotModelAGeneric
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVGenericRobotModelA
#. TOPIC: 010D246F
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_GenericModelA_Hellos01
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "0132C2"
msgid "If you have issues to report, please direct your query to the nearest security officer."
msgstr "신고 사항이 있으면 제일 가까운 경비대원에게 직접 문의하십시오."

#. VOICE TYPE: RobotModelAGeneric
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVGenericRobotModelA
#. TOPIC: 010D246F
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_GenericModelA_Hellos01
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "0132C1"
msgid "For healing, please consult Hanton Irara at the Halls of Healing."
msgstr "치료를 원하시면, 회복의 전당에서 핸톤 이라라와 상담하십시오."

#. VOICE TYPE: RobotModelAGeneric
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVGenericRobotModelA
#. TOPIC: 010D246F
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_GenericModelA_Hellos01
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "0132C0"
msgid "Please note: all Ministry buildings were in the radius of the cataclysm and are no longer available."
msgstr "알립니다. 대재난 당시 범위 안에 있던 정부 건물들은 더 이상 접근하실 수 없습니다."

#. VOICE TYPE: RobotModelAGeneric
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVGenericRobotModelA
#. TOPIC: 010D246F
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_GenericModelA_Hellos01
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "0132BF"
msgid "Please be advised that areas near the Scaled Citadel may be hazardous."
msgstr "비늘 성채 부근 지역은 위험할 수도 있음을 주지합니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: He sounds plenty lost himself. &&& Malibor: You... could hear him? &&& Malibor: Despite the sightings, none have heard a word from Anasko in all this time. Yet you claim to?|Do not toy with me. Not about this. If you speak truth, you must prove it. What did he say?
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Malibor: By the Serpent...
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ02
#. TOPIC: 0102F717
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ02_Stage400_MaliborScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132BE"
msgid "All Must Serve."
msgstr "모두가 섬겨야 한다."

#. VOICE TYPE: RobotModelAGeneric
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVGenericRobotModelA
#. TOPIC: 010D246F
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_GenericModelA_Hellos01
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "0132BD"
msgid "Move along, please."
msgstr "계속 움직이십시오."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_VaruunGenericMale01
#. FACE: Angry
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVGenericPhantom
#. TOPIC: 010E343B
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_PhantomTaunt
#. TYPE: Combat
#. SUBTYPE: Taunt
msgctxt "0132BC"
msgid "Who's there? I see nothing!"
msgstr "거기 누구야? 아무것도 안 보여!"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Angry
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_VaruunGenericMale01
#. FACE: Angry
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVGenericPhantom
#. TOPIC: 010E343B
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_PhantomTaunt
#. TYPE: Combat
#. SUBTYPE: Taunt
msgctxt "0132BB"
msgid "Get away from me!"
msgstr "내게서 떨어져라!"

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to AzadDubas
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: AzadDubas: When my wife and I first moved out here, it was for practical reasons.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E5
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLRemote
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132BA"
msgid "This place seems pretty remote. Do you want to live away from other people?"
msgstr "여긴 꽤 외진 곳 같네요. 다른 사람들과 떨어져서 살고 싶으셨나요?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: This place seems pretty remote. Do you want to live away from other people?
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E4
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLRemote
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132B9"
msgid "When my wife and I first moved out here, it was for practical reasons."
msgstr "아내와 제가 처음 여기로 이사 온 건 현실적인 이유 때문이었죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E4
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLRemote
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132B8"
msgid "It allowed us to observe the plants and creatures we study in their natural habitat."
msgstr "저희가 연구하는 동식물을 자연 서식지에서 관찰할 수 있었거든요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E4
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLRemote
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132B7"
msgid "Having said that, I've grown very fond of the peace, quiet and solitude that we enjoy here."
msgstr "그러다가, 이곳에서 누리는 평화, 고요, 고독이 아주 마음에 들게 됐죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E4
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLRemote
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132B6"
msgid "I don't think I could return to the city now. I'm sure I'd find it too noisy and distracting."
msgstr "이제는 도시로 돌아갈 수 없을 것 같습니다. 너무 시끄럽고 산만해서 못 견딜 겁니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to AzadDubas
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: AzadDubas: I suppose in some ways. it's much the same as in other cultures.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E3
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132B5"
msgid "What place does science have in Va'ruun society?"
msgstr "바룬 사회에서 과학의 지위는 어떤가요?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What place does science have in Va'ruun society?
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E2
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132B4"
msgid "I suppose in some ways. it's much the same as in other cultures."
msgstr "어떤 면에서는 다른 문화권과 비슷하다고 생각합니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E2
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132B3"
msgid "We seek a greater understanding of our world through observation and reason."
msgstr "저희는 관찰과 이성을 통해 세상을 더 잘 이해하려고 노력하죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: You're right, it's not really that different.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E2
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132B2"
msgid "We do this work in service to the people, that all may benefit."
msgstr "저희는 신민들 모두가 혜택을 누릴 수 있도록 하기 위해, 이 일을 하는 겁니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What place does science have in Va'ruun society? &&& AzadDubas: I suppose in some ways. it's much the same as in other cultures.|We seek a greater understanding of our world through observation and reason.|We do this work in service to the people, that all may benefit.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I'm sure our beliefs and customs must seem unusual to those not raised within our way of life.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E1
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132B1"
msgid "You're right, it's not really that different."
msgstr "맞아요. 사실 다른 문화권도 그렇게 다르지는 않죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What place does science have in Va'ruun society? &&& AzadDubas: I suppose in some ways. it's much the same as in other cultures.|We seek a greater understanding of our world through observation and reason.|We do this work in service to the people, that all may benefit.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I suppose I've always thought of the Great Serpent as a teacher and a guide.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DF
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132B0"
msgid "Interesting that you didn't say anything about the Great Serpent there."
msgstr "의외로 위대한 뱀에 대해 아무 말도 하지 않다니 흥미롭네요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: You're right, it's not really that different.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: You're right, it's not really that different.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E0
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132AF"
msgid "I'm sure our beliefs and customs must seem unusual to those not raised within our way of life."
msgstr "우리의 믿음과 관습은 우리와 다른 방식으로 자란 사람들에게는 이상하게 보일 거라 생각합니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: You're right, it's not really that different.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I see no reason they can't coexist.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E0
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132AE"
msgid "Be that as it may, we are not really all that different in how we experience life."
msgstr "그렇다고 해도, 삶을 경험하는 방식이 그렇게 다르지는 않죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: I see no reason they can't coexist.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: I see no reason they can't coexist.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132AD"
msgid "Then we're of one mind on the subject."
msgstr "그럼 우리의 의견이 일치한 거 같군요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Emphasis on "must" / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: I see no reason they can't coexist.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132AC"
msgid "I'll go even further and say that they must coexist, for both are vital in any successful civilization."
msgstr "저는 한 단계 더 나아가서 그 둘이 공존해야 한다고 말하고 싶네요. 번성한 문명이라면 어디든 그 둘은 매우 중요할 테니까요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: You're right, it's not really that different. &&& AzadDubas: I'm sure our beliefs and customs must seem unusual to those not raised within our way of life.|Be that as it may, we are not really all that different in how we experience life.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Then we're of one mind on the subject.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DB
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132AB"
msgid "I see no reason they can't coexist."
msgstr "저는 그 둘이 왜 공존할 수 없다는 건지 모르겠어요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: And that doesn't conflict with your faith in any way? &&& AzadDubas: For me they do not, no.|Some doubt the value of our work, and others consider science to be nearly a cousin to heresy.|I suppose there are many perspectives regarding the coexistence of faith and science.|What about you? Do you believe that faith and science sit in contradiction to one another?
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Ah, you share that point of view with my wife.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D7
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132AA"
msgid "Science can be useful, but only faith can truly unlock the deepest mysteries of the universe."
msgstr "과학은 유용하긴 하지만, 오직 신앙만이 우주의 가장 깊은 신비를 진정으로 풀어낼 수 있죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Interesting that you didn't say anything about the Great Serpent there.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Interesting that you didn't say anything about the Great Serpent there.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DE
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132A9"
msgid "I suppose I've always thought of the Great Serpent as a teacher and a guide."
msgstr "저는 항상 위대한 뱀 님을 스승이자 인도자라고 생각하고 있습니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Interesting that you didn't say anything about the Great Serpent there.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DE
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132A8"
msgid "He is not here to solve all of our problems and mysteries, but rather to empower us to solve them."
msgstr ""
"위대한 뱀 님은 우리의 모든 문제와 신비를 해결하기 위해 여기 있는 것이 아니라, 우리가 그것을 해결할 수 있도록 힘을 주시는 분이시죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Interesting that you didn't say anything about the Great Serpent there.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DE
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132A7"
msgid "Our path is illuminated by the Serpent's wisdom, it is true."
msgstr "우리의 길이 위대한 뱀 님의 지혜로 밝혀지는 것은 사실입니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Interesting that you didn't say anything about the Great Serpent there.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Faith is a relic of human history. It's science that will take us into the future.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DE
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132A6"
msgid "But our achievements are the fruits of our effort as individuals."
msgstr "하지만 우리의 업적은 개인으로서의 노력의 결실입니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What place does science have in Va'ruun society? &&& AzadDubas: I suppose in some ways. it's much the same as in other cultures.|We seek a greater understanding of our world through observation and reason.|We do this work in service to the people, that all may benefit.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: It must be comforting to have a mind so filled with certainty and so free of questions.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D5
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132A5"
msgid "The question is irrelevant. Devotion to the Great Serpent is all that matters."
msgstr "그 질문은 요점에서 벗어났습니다. 위대한 뱀에 대한 헌신만이 중요할 뿐입니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: And that doesn't conflict with your faith in any way?
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: And that doesn't conflict with your faith in any way?
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DC
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132A4"
msgid "For me they do not, no."
msgstr "저에게 둘은 서로 상충하지 않습니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: And that doesn't conflict with your faith in any way?
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DC
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132A3"
msgid "Some doubt the value of our work, and others consider science to be nearly a cousin to heresy."
msgstr "어떤 이들은 저희가 하는 일이 가치가 있는지 의구심을 품고, 또 어떤 이들은 과학이 거의 이단의 사촌쯤 된다고 여기죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: And that doesn't conflict with your faith in any way?
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DC
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132A2"
msgid "I suppose there are many perspectives regarding the coexistence of faith and science."
msgstr "신앙과 과학의 공존에 대해서는 다양한 관점이 있을 거라 생각해요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: And that doesn't conflict with your faith in any way?
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Science can be useful, but only faith can truly unlock the deepest mysteries of the universe.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DC
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132A1"
msgid "What about you? Do you believe that faith and science sit in contradiction to one another?"
msgstr "당신은 어떻습니까? 신앙과 과학이 서로 모순된다고 생각하십니까?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Science can be useful, but only faith can truly unlock the deepest mysteries of the universe.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Science can be useful, but only faith can truly unlock the deepest mysteries of the universe.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D6
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0132A0"
msgid "Ah, you share that point of view with my wife."
msgstr "아, 당신은 제 아내와 같은 관점을 가지고 있군요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Science can be useful, but only faith can truly unlock the deepest mysteries of the universe.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D6
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01329F"
msgid "In truth, I don't disagree. I'm convinced there is a grand design behind life's vast complexity."
msgstr "사실, 저도 동의해요. 저는 생명의 광대한 복잡성 뒤에 위대한 설계가 있다고 확신합니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Science can be useful, but only faith can truly unlock the deepest mysteries of the universe.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D6
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01329E"
msgid "If, by grasping to understand even a fraction of it, we can help our people, then we must."
msgstr "그것의 극히 일부라도 이해함으로써 우리 신민들을 도울 수 있다면, 저희는 그렇게 해야만 해요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: What place does science have in Va'ruun society? &&& AzadDubas: I suppose in some ways. it's much the same as in other cultures.|We seek a greater understanding of our world through observation and reason.|We do this work in service to the people, that all may benefit.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: For me they do not, no.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9DD
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01329D"
msgid "And that doesn't conflict with your faith in any way?"
msgstr "그럼 과학이 당신의 신앙과 어떻게든 상충하진 않나요?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Interesting that you didn't say anything about the Great Serpent there. &&& AzadDubas: I suppose I've always thought of the Great Serpent as a teacher and a guide.|He is not here to solve all of our problems and mysteries, but rather to empower us to solve them.|Our path is illuminated by the Serpent's wisdom, it is true.|But our achievements are the fruits of our effort as individuals.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: Science has opened our eyes to vital discoveries. Consider medicine and exploration, for example.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D9
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01329C"
msgid "Faith is a relic of human history. It's science that will take us into the future."
msgstr "신앙은 인류사의 유물일 뿐입니다. 우리를 미래로 이끄는 것은 바로 과학이죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to SherineDubas
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SherineDubas: What a delightful question! I'm so glad you asked. You see, it's something of a point of pride.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D3
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLBuilt
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01329B"
msgid "Who built this place?"
msgstr "이 기지는 누가 지었나요?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Happy, eager to share the details / Happy / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Who built this place?
#. ALIAS: SherineDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSherineDubas
#. FACE: Happy
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D2
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLBuilt
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01329A"
msgid "What a delightful question! I'm so glad you asked. You see, it's something of a point of pride."
msgstr "정말 반가운 질문이네요! 물어봐 주셔서 정말 기뻐요. 이 기지는 제 자랑거리거든요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Proud / Friendly / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: SherineDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSherineDubas
#. FACE: Friendly
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D2
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLBuilt
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013299"
msgid "It was my mother who designed the layout for Hamadi Station."
msgstr "저희 어머니가 하마디 기지를 설계하셨어요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Proud, happy / Friendly / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: SherineDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSherineDubas
#. FACE: Friendly
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D2
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLBuilt
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013298"
msgid "She was a gifted architect as well as a botanist, and yet still found the time to be a wonderful mother."
msgstr "어머니는 뛰어난 건축가이자 식물학자 셨지만, 짬을 내셔서 훌륭한 어머니 역할도 잘 해내셨죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: SherineDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSherineDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D2
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLBuilt
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013297"
msgid "She married an engineer and they built this place together."
msgstr "어머니는 엔지니어셨던 아버지와 결혼하셨고, 두 분이 함께 이곳을 지으셨어요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: SherineDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFSherineDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D2
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLBuilt
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013296"
msgid "Hamadi was my father's family name."
msgstr "하마디는 제 아버지의 성씨였어요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to SherineDubas
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: SherineDubas: By the grace of the Serpent, we were spared.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D1
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_SherineTLCalamity
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013295"
msgid "How are you coping with the recent calamity in the city?"
msgstr "최근 도시에서 있었던 재난에 어떻게 대처하고 계신가요?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: The question is irrelevant. Devotion to the Great Serpent is all that matters. 
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: The question is irrelevant. Devotion to the Great Serpent is all that matters. 
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D4
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013294"
msgid "It must be comforting to have a mind so filled with certainty and so free of questions."
msgstr "의심이라고는 없이 확신만 가득 찬 머리를 갖고 산다면, 참 편하긴 하겠군요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: The question is irrelevant. Devotion to the Great Serpent is all that matters. 
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D4
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013293"
msgid "Alas, that is a comfort I will never know."
msgstr "안타깝게도, 저는 그런 위안을 결코 알 수 없을 거에요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Faith is a relic of human history. It's science that will take us into the future.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Faith is a relic of human history. It's science that will take us into the future.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D8
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013292"
msgid "Science has opened our eyes to vital discoveries. Consider medicine and exploration, for example."
msgstr "과학은 우리가 매우 중요한 발견을 할 수 있게 해줬지요. 예를 들어, 의학과 탐험을 생각해 보시죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Faith is a relic of human history. It's science that will take us into the future.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D8
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013291"
msgid "And yet I think faith has great value as well."
msgstr "하지만 저는 신앙 역시 큰 가치가 있다고 생각해요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Faith is a relic of human history. It's science that will take us into the future.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D8
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013290"
msgid "Faith provides moral guidance, traditions that bind society together and hope in dark times."
msgstr "신앙은 도덕적 지침을 제공하고, 사회를 하나로 묶는 전통을 만들어주며, 암담한 시기에 희망을 주죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Faith is a relic of human history. It's science that will take us into the future.
#. ALIAS: AzadDubas
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMAzadDubas
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation
#. TOPIC: 0110A9D8
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_DialogueHamadiStation_AzadTLScience
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01328F"
msgid "Without it, I think we would be a lost and soulless people."
msgstr "신앙이 없었다면, 우리는 길도 잃고 영혼도 잃어버린 신민이 되었을 거예요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Question / to Speaker
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Vethaal_Lovek: I speak the truth. And if such truth came to light, surely our Speaker would not tolerate such treachery, hm? &&& Speaker: No. He would not. In fact, he would impale such traitors on the peak of the Scaled Citadel itself. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: If I may, I'd argue this debate is a question of law. Where is the line drawn?|Obviously, if the accused is found guilty, then they deserve the harshest of punishments. If there is any doubt, however... &&& Speaker: Doubt does not exist when you are the mouth of the Great Serpent. If I proclaim someone a Zealot, then that is what they are.
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Question
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Then this matter is closed. Let us move to the next item on the agenda.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B5B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_020_CouncilMeetings_Scene02
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01328E"
msgid "I apologize speaker, I meant no offense."
msgstr "죄송합니다, 대변자님. 악의는 없었습니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: Be that as it may, House Veth'aal would like to offer House Dul'kehf priority here. We empathize with your loss of home and will patiently wait for our turn. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Your accusation is baseless, Mediary. There is no evidence of any such theft. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: Regardless, the act is suspicious. Whereas our house has demonstrated its commitment to service by staying at the Keep.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMViktorVethaal
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B59
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01328D"
msgid "Agreed. Construction will begin with House Veth'aal, followed by the Ministry of State."
msgstr "동감이다. 베타알 가문 저택부터 건설을 시작하고, 그다음은 국무성으로 하겠다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMViktorVethaal
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Then it will be done. If all have spoken their piece, let us move on to the next item.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B59
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01328C"
msgid "House Dul'kehf, and all the other branches of the Halls of Authority, come secondary."
msgstr "둘케프 가문과 권위의 전당에 속한 모든 지부들은 부수적으로 고려할 것이다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: Be that as it may, House Veth'aal would like to offer House Dul'kehf priority here. We empathize with your loss of home and will patiently wait for our turn. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Your accusation is baseless, Mediary. There is no evidence of any such theft. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: Regardless, the act is suspicious. Whereas our house has demonstrated its commitment to service by staying at the Keep.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFRazmaKadic
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Then it will be done. If all have spoken their piece, let us move on to the next item.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B59
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01328B"
msgid "Motive aside, the Heralds are inconvenienced by House Dul'kehf's presence. They will receive priority over House Veth'aal."
msgstr "동기는 그렇다 치고, 전령들은 둘케프 가문을 불편하게 여기고 있어. 전령들이 베타알 가문보다 우선권을 받게 될 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: Be that as it may, House Veth'aal would like to offer House Dul'kehf priority here. We empathize with your loss of home and will patiently wait for our turn. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Your accusation is baseless, Mediary. There is no evidence of any such theft. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: Regardless, the act is suspicious. Whereas our house has demonstrated its commitment to service by staying at the Keep.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMHasmakDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Then it will be done. If all have spoken their piece, let us move on to the next item.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B59
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01328A"
msgid "Very well, Mediary. I accept your offering."
msgstr "알겠네, 중개자. 자네 제안을 수락하지."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: Then it will be done. If all have spoken their piece, let us move on to the next item.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B57
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013289"
msgid "Then it will be done. That appears to be the last item on the agenda for today."
msgstr "그러면 끝났군요. 오늘은 그게 마지막 안건인 것 같습니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Dulkehf_Malibor
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker:  &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: We should discuss the displacement of the noble Houses. |I motion to make House Dul'kehf a priority. Sharing occupancy with the Halls of Healing is not ideal for us or the Heralds.
#. ALIAS: Kadic_Djimal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDjimalKadic
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: Be that as it may, House Veth'aal would like to offer House Dul'kehf priority here. We empathize with your loss of home and will patiently wait for our turn.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B56
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013288"
msgid "I'd remind the Mediary that your House chose that location. This is a problem of your own making."
msgstr "그쪽 가문에서 고른 장소라는 걸 중개자에게 상기시키고 싶군요. 그건 그쪽에서 만들어낸 문제죠."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker: 
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B5A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013287"
msgid "We should discuss the displacement of the noble Houses."
msgstr "명문 가문들의 이주 문제를 논의해야 합니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Vethaal_Lovek
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Kadic_Djimal: I'd remind the Mediary that your House chose that location. This is a problem of your own making.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B5A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013286"
msgid "I motion to make House Dul'kehf a priority. Sharing occupancy with the Halls of Healing is not ideal for us or the Heralds."
msgstr "둘케프 가문을 우선순위로 하지요. 회복의 전당을 계속 공유하는 건 우리에게나 전령님에게나 좋은 일이 아닙니다."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: Your accusation is baseless, Mediary. There is no evidence of any such theft. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: Regardless, the act is suspicious. Whereas our house has demonstrated its commitment to service by staying at the Keep. &&& Speaker: Agreed. Construction will begin with House Veth'aal, followed by the Ministry of State.|House Dul'kehf, and all the other branches of the Halls of Authority, come secondary.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Then it will be done. That appears to be the last item on the agenda for today.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B58
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013285"
msgid "Then it will be done. If all have spoken their piece, let us move on to the next item."
msgstr "그러면 끝났군요. 모두 발언을 마치셨다면, 다음 항목으로 넘어가겠습니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Here, Hasmak Dul'kehf has been appointed Speaker. Lovek knows arguing the point is moot, so he tries to make it seem like he's graciously deferring. / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker:  &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: We should discuss the displacement of the noble Houses. |I motion to make House Dul'kehf a priority. Sharing occupancy with the Halls of Healing is not ideal for us or the Heralds. &&& Kadic_Djimal: I'd remind the Mediary that your House chose that location. This is a problem of your own making.
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Your accusation is baseless, Mediary. There is no evidence of any such theft.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B55
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013284"
msgid "Be that as it may, House Veth'aal would like to offer House Dul'kehf priority here. We empathize with your loss of home and will patiently wait for our turn."
msgstr ""
"그렇기는 하지만, 베타알 가문은 둘케프 가문에게 우선권을 주고 싶소이다. 집을 잃은 아픔에 공감하는 바이니, 인내심을 가지고 우리 차례를 "
"기다리겠소."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: In this version, House Dul'kehf is not in charge, so Lovek argues his house should be built first. / Stern / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker:  &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: We should discuss the displacement of the noble Houses. |I motion to make House Dul'kehf a priority. Sharing occupancy with the Halls of Healing is not ideal for us or the Heralds. &&& Kadic_Djimal: I'd remind the Mediary that your House chose that location. This is a problem of your own making.
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Stern
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B55
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013283"
msgid "House Veth'aal seconds that. We chose the Keep as it made the most sense."
msgstr "베타알 가문도 동의하오. 우리는 가장 합리적으로 성채를 골랐소."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Your accusation is baseless, Mediary. There is no evidence of any such theft.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B55
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_030_CouncilMeetings_Scene03
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013282"
msgid "House Dul'kehf, meanwhile, chose to strategically hoard medical supplies. They should not be rewarded for such actions."
msgstr "그 반면 둘케프 가문은 전략적으로 의료 용품을 비축하기로 결정했지. 그런 행동에 보상이 있어서는 안 되오."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker:  &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Continuing on from a previous discussion, let us discuss the state of the refugee camp. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: As the House in charge of employment, the Ministry of State continues to monitor the situation, and fill needs where necessary.
#. ALIAS: Kadic_Djimal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDjimalKadic
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: With all due respect, Mediary, we cannot fit square pegs into a round hole.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B51
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013281"
msgid "At a speed that is not acceptable. The conditions there are brutal. We must do what we can to ameliorate them."
msgstr "용납할 수 없는 속도로 말이죠. 난민촌 상황은 처참해요. 상황을 개선하려면 뭐라도 해야 한다고요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Kadic_Djimal: At a speed that is not acceptable. The conditions there are brutal. We must do what we can to ameliorate them. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: With all due respect, Mediary, we cannot fit square pegs into a round hole.|A farmer cannot serve where a mechanic is required.
#. ALIAS: Kadic_Djimal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDjimalKadic
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: And how much time will that take? Not to mention there's no guarantee these people are even capable.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013280"
msgid "Then train them. Don't sit on your hands and do nothing."
msgstr "그럼 훈련을 시켜요. 손 놓고 앉아만 있지 말고요."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: Moving on. Let us proceed to the next item on the agenda.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B52
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01327F"
msgid "Not to interrupt, but it appears we are out of time."
msgstr "방해하려는 건 아닙니다만, 시간이 다 된 것 같군요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker:  &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Continuing on from a previous discussion, let us discuss the state of the refugee camp.
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Kadic_Djimal: At a speed that is not acceptable. The conditions there are brutal. We must do what we can to ameliorate them.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B50
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01327E"
msgid "As the House in charge of employment, the Ministry of State continues to monitor the situation, and fill needs where necessary."
msgstr "국무성은 고용 부문을 책임지는 가문으로서 상황을 지속적으로 모니터링하고, 필요한 부분을 채우고 있소이다."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: There is precedence, given recent events, and additional hands are very much needed. &&& ...  &&& Kadic_Djimal: They would be closely vetted, and their behavior monitored. In fact, you can do it personally, Mediary.|Unless you doubt the Ministry of State's capability to do so? &&& Vethaal_Lovek: House Veth'aal will do its duty, as it always has. &&& Speaker: Enough. As Speaker, it is my responsibility to protect the citizens of Dazra.|This "proposal" flies in the face of that edict. I will not consider it.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: And on that note, it appears we are out of time.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B49
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01327D"
msgid "Understood. Let us then move on to the next item on the agenda."
msgstr "알겠습니다. 그러면 다음 안건으로 넘어가겠습니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker:  &&& Kadic_Djimal: I'd like to bring up the subject of immigration.|As you all know, we have agents all across the Settled Systems, which include people from outside Va'ruun'kai.|It's my belief that many of these people would be willing to serve House Va'ruun and become Promised. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: There is precedence, given recent events, and additional hands are very much needed.
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Kadic_Djimal: They would be closely vetted, and their behavior monitored. In fact, you can do it personally, Mediary.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B46
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01327C"
msgid "I strongly disagree. Our city is in a state of chaos, and you would bring our enemies to our front door? No, I cannot abide."
msgstr "난 단호히 반대하오. 우리 도시가 혼란스러운 상황인데, 우리의 적을 문 앞에 들여놓겠다니? 이건 용납 못 하겠소."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: With all due respect, Mediary, we cannot fit square pegs into a round hole.|A farmer cannot serve where a mechanic is required. &&& Kadic_Djimal: Then train them. Don't sit on your hands and do nothing. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: And how much time will that take? Not to mention there's no guarantee these people are even capable.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMViktorVethaal
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: As you command, Speaker.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013279"
msgid "We will not waste time training the weak. If they are unwilling to serve, they must be culled."
msgstr "약자를 훈련시키는 데 시간을 낭비하지는 않겠다. 섬길 의지가 없는 자들은 도태되어야 한다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: With all due respect, Mediary, we cannot fit square pegs into a round hole.|A farmer cannot serve where a mechanic is required. &&& Kadic_Djimal: Then train them. Don't sit on your hands and do nothing. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: And how much time will that take? Not to mention there's no guarantee these people are even capable.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFRazmaKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: As you command, Speaker.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013278"
msgid "My sister is right. You are wasting time by keeping these people idle. Have security start a survey and find out where they can be useful."
msgstr ""
"내 동생 말이 맞아. 신민들을 그냥 놀리는 건 시간 낭비야. 경비대를 시켜서 신민들을 유용하게 쓸 만한 곳이 없는지 살펴보도록 해."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: With all due respect, Mediary, we cannot fit square pegs into a round hole.|A farmer cannot serve where a mechanic is required. &&& Kadic_Djimal: Then train them. Don't sit on your hands and do nothing. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: And how much time will that take? Not to mention there's no guarantee these people are even capable.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMHasmakDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013277"
msgid "Perhaps the issue can be resolved by casting a wider net. Find additional areas of need where individuals can assist."
msgstr "생각을 더 넓혀보면 문제를 해결할 수 있을지도 모르네. 개인들이 도움을 줄 수 있을만한 영역이 있는지 찾아보게나."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMHasmakDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: As you command, Speaker.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013276"
msgid "A farmer cannot be a mechanic, but they can hand one a wrench."
msgstr "농부가 정비사가 될 순 없겠지만, 렌치를 건네줄 수는 있겠지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Question
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Vethaal_Lovek: With all due respect, Mediary, we cannot fit square pegs into a round hole.|A farmer cannot serve where a mechanic is required. &&& Kadic_Djimal: Then train them. Don't sit on your hands and do nothing.
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Question
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Speaker: We will not waste time training the weak. If they are unwilling to serve, they must be culled.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013275"
msgid "And how much time will that take? Not to mention there's no guarantee these people are even capable."
msgstr "시간이 얼마나 걸릴 줄 알고 말이오? 신민들에게 훈련받을 능력이 있을지도 장담 못 한다는 건 말할 필요도 없고."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Vethaal_Lovek: I strongly disagree. Our city is in a state of chaos, and you would bring our enemies to our front door? No, I cannot abide. &&& Kadic_Djimal: They would be closely vetted, and their behavior monitored. In fact, you can do it personally, Mediary.|Unless you doubt the Ministry of State's capability to do so?
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Speaker: Enough. As Speaker, it is my responsibility to protect the citizens of Dazra.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B42
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013274"
msgid "House Veth'aal will do its duty, as it always has."
msgstr "베타알 가문은 늘 그래왔듯이 소임을 다할 것이외다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious / to Speaker, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker: 
#. ALIAS: Kadic_Djimal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDjimalKadic
#. FACE: Serious
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4A
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013273"
msgid "I'd like to bring up the subject of immigration."
msgstr "이주 문제를 논의해보고 싶군요."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: Understood. Let us then move on to the next item on the agenda.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B48
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013272"
msgid "And on that note, it appears we are out of time."
msgstr "그리고 말 나온 김에, 시간이 다 된 것 같군요."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Kadic_Djimal: I'd like to bring up the subject of immigration.|As you all know, we have agents all across the Settled Systems, which include people from outside Va'ruun'kai.|It's my belief that many of these people would be willing to serve House Va'ruun and become Promised. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: There is precedence, given recent events, and additional hands are very much needed. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: I strongly disagree. Our city is in a state of chaos, and you would bring our enemies to our front door? No, I cannot abide.
#. ALIAS: Kadic_Djimal
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFDjimalKadic
#. FACE: Defiant
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B47
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013271"
msgid "They would be closely vetted, and their behavior monitored. In fact, you can do it personally, Mediary."
msgstr "면밀하게 심사할 거고, 행동도 계속 관찰할 거예요. 솔직히 개인적으로도 할 수 있는 일이잖아요, 중개자님."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker: Nonsense. The more ships we ransack, the more our supplies increase. It is a problem that solves itself. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Understood. If that concludes the matter, let us move to the next item on the agenda. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Understood. And it seems we are out of time.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFRazmaKadic
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109851
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_999_CouncilMeetings_End
#. INFO GROUP: FormID 01109860
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013270"
msgid "Then we will assemble at a later date. All Must Serve."
msgstr "그럼 나중에 다시 모이도록 하지. 모두가 섬겨야 한다."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker: Nonsense. The more ships we ransack, the more our supplies increase. It is a problem that solves itself. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Understood. If that concludes the matter, let us move to the next item on the agenda. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Understood. And it seems we are out of time.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFRazmaKadic
#. FACE: Confident
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109851
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_999_CouncilMeetings_End
#. INFO GROUP: FormID 01109860
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01326F"
msgid "Then the meeting is adjourned. Let us continue this discussion another time."
msgstr "그럼 회의는 이만 마치지. 이 논의는 다음에 계속하도록 해."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Suspicious / to Kadic_Djimal
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Vethaal_Lovek: As the House in charge of employment, the Ministry of State continues to monitor the situation, and fill needs where necessary. &&& Kadic_Djimal: At a speed that is not acceptable. The conditions there are brutal. We must do what we can to ameliorate them.
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Suspicious
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01326E"
msgid "With all due respect, Mediary, we cannot fit square pegs into a round hole."
msgstr "이런 말 해서 미안하지만, 중개자. 네모난 못을 둥근 구멍에 넣을 순 없소."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Kadic_Djimal: Then train them. Don't sit on your hands and do nothing.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01326D"
msgid "A farmer cannot serve where a mechanic is required."
msgstr "농부는 정비사가 필요한 자리에서 섬길 수 없단 말이오."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: Continuing on from a previous discussion, let us discuss the state of the refugee camp. &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: And how much time will that take? Not to mention there's no guarantee these people are even capable. &&& Speaker: We will not waste time training the weak. If they are unwilling to serve, they must be culled. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: As you command, Speaker.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Not to interrupt, but it appears we are out of time.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B53
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01326C"
msgid "Moving on. Let us proceed to the next item on the agenda."
msgstr "계속 진행하지요. 다음 안건으로 넘어가겠습니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: I strongly disagree. Our city is in a state of chaos, and you would bring our enemies to our front door? No, I cannot abide. &&& Kadic_Djimal: They would be closely vetted, and their behavior monitored. In fact, you can do it personally, Mediary.|Unless you doubt the Ministry of State's capability to do so? &&& Vethaal_Lovek: House Veth'aal will do its duty, as it always has.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMViktorVethaal
#. FACE: Defiant
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B44
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01326B"
msgid "Enough. As Speaker, it is my responsibility to protect the citizens of Dazra."
msgstr "그만. 나는 대변자로서 다즈라 시민들을 보호할 책임이 있다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: I strongly disagree. Our city is in a state of chaos, and you would bring our enemies to our front door? No, I cannot abide. &&& Kadic_Djimal: They would be closely vetted, and their behavior monitored. In fact, you can do it personally, Mediary.|Unless you doubt the Ministry of State's capability to do so? &&& Vethaal_Lovek: House Veth'aal will do its duty, as it always has.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFRazmaKadic
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Understood. Let us then move on to the next item on the agenda.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B44
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01326A"
msgid "Then we'll begin the vetting process. And Lovek, rest assured, if you find any bad actors among the bunch, I will remove their heads personally."
msgstr ""
"그럼 심사 절차를 시작하도록 하지. 그리고 로벡. 걱정하지 마. 만약 그중에서 불순분자를 발견하게 된다면, 내가 직접 목을 칠 테니까."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Serious / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: I strongly disagree. Our city is in a state of chaos, and you would bring our enemies to our front door? No, I cannot abide. &&& Kadic_Djimal: They would be closely vetted, and their behavior monitored. In fact, you can do it personally, Mediary.|Unless you doubt the Ministry of State's capability to do so? &&& Vethaal_Lovek: House Veth'aal will do its duty, as it always has.
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMHasmakDulkehf
#. FACE: Serious
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B44
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_050_CouncilMeetings_Scene05
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013269"
msgid "Without committing, I will say the bar for citizenship will be much higher than the one for smugglers and others we have integrated."
msgstr "말할 필요도 없겠지만, 시민권 기준은 밀수업자나 우리에게 이미 통합된 이들보다 훨씬 더 높아질 걸세."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: Then this matter is closed. Let us move to the next item on the agenda.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110984C
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_020_CouncilMeetings_Scene02
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013267"
msgid "Then this matter is closed. And on that note, it seems we are out of time."
msgstr "그럼 이 문제는 종결됐군요. 그러고 보니, 시간이 다 된 것 같습니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Vethaal_Lovek: It's time to take a stance on all who support Jandar's teachings. We must root them out from the inside before the poison spreads. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: Are you implying, Mediary, that there are Zealot sympathizers among us?
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Kadic_Djimal: You speak blasphemy!
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109849
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_020_CouncilMeetings_Scene02
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013266"
msgid "I am not implying. I know this for a fact. Some have even said our noble Houses may be aiding a few."
msgstr "떠 보는 게 아니오. 사실이니까. 심지어는 우리 명문 가문들이 몇 놈을 도와준다는 이야기까지 있소."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker: 
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: As the House in charge of employment, the Ministry of State continues to monitor the situation, and fill needs where necessary.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B54
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013265"
msgid "Continuing on from a previous discussion, let us discuss the state of the refugee camp."
msgstr "이전 논의에 이어서, 난민촌 현황에 대해 논의하겠습니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker: I'm not sure what you're implying, Mediary. But it can't be good for your career, or your health. &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: If I may, I'd argue this debate is a question of law. Where is the line drawn?|Obviously, if the accused is found guilty, then they deserve the harshest of punishments. If there is any doubt, however...
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFRazmaKadic
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: I apologize speaker, I meant no offense.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110984F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_020_CouncilMeetings_Scene02
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013264"
msgid "It is not a matter of doubt, it is a matter of resources. We do not have time to investigate every whisper in the wind."
msgstr "이건 의혹의 문제가 아니라 자원의 문제야. 세간에 떠도는 소문을 전부 조사하고 있을 시간은 없어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker: House Dul'kehf has never been a friend to the Zealots.  &&& Dulkehf_Malibor: If I may, I'd argue this debate is a question of law. Where is the line drawn?|Obviously, if the accused is found guilty, then they deserve the harshest of punishments. If there is any doubt, however...
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMHasmakDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Vethaal_Lovek: I apologize speaker, I meant no offense.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110984F
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_020_CouncilMeetings_Scene02
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013263"
msgid "Precisely. Either House Veth'aal should name the accused, or end this meaningless exercise in thought."
msgstr "바로 그거지. 베타알 가문에서 용의자의 이름을 밝히지 않을 거라면, 이런 무의미한 논쟁은 입 밖에 내지 말게."

#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: If I may, I'd argue this debate is a question of law. Where is the line drawn?|Obviously, if the accused is found guilty, then they deserve the harshest of punishments. If there is any doubt, however... &&& Speaker: Doubt does not exist when you are the mouth of the Great Serpent. If I proclaim someone a Zealot, then that is what they are. &&& Vethaal_Lovek: I apologize speaker, I meant no offense.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Then this matter is closed. And on that note, it seems we are out of time.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110984D
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_020_CouncilMeetings_Scene02
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013262"
msgid "Then this matter is closed. Let us move to the next item on the agenda."
msgstr "그럼 이 문제는 종결됐군요. 다음 안건으로 넘어가겠습니다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: I am not implying. I know this for a fact. Some have even said our noble Houses may be aiding a few. &&& Kadic_Djimal: You speak blasphemy! &&& Vethaal_Lovek: I speak the truth. And if such truth came to light, surely our Speaker would not tolerate such treachery, hm?
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFRazmaKadic
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: If I may, I'd argue this debate is a question of law. Where is the line drawn?
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110984E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_020_CouncilMeetings_Scene02
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013260"
msgid "I'm not sure what you're implying, Mediary. But it can't be good for your career, or your health."
msgstr "무슨 뜻으로 하는 말인지 잘 모르겠군, 중개자. 일단 그대의 경력이나 건강에는 좋지 않은 말 같은데."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& ...  &&& Vethaal_Lovek: I am not implying. I know this for a fact. Some have even said our noble Houses may be aiding a few. &&& Kadic_Djimal: You speak blasphemy! &&& Vethaal_Lovek: I speak the truth. And if such truth came to light, surely our Speaker would not tolerate such treachery, hm?
#. ALIAS: Speaker
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMHasmakDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: If I may, I'd argue this debate is a question of law. Where is the line drawn?
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110984E
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_020_CouncilMeetings_Scene02
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01325F"
msgid "House Dul'kehf has never been a friend to the Zealots."
msgstr "둘케프 가문은 광신도의 친구였던 적이 한 번도 없다네."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Neutral / to Speaker, Vethaal_Lovek
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Dulkehf_Malibor: Are you implying, Mediary, that there are Zealot sympathizers among us? &&& ...  &&& Kadic_Djimal: You speak blasphemy! &&& Vethaal_Lovek: I speak the truth. And if such truth came to light, surely our Speaker would not tolerate such treachery, hm? &&& Speaker: No. He would not. In fact, he would impale such traitors on the peak of the Scaled Citadel itself.
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109846
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_020_CouncilMeetings_Scene02
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01325E"
msgid "If I may, I'd argue this debate is a question of law. Where is the line drawn?"
msgstr "한 말씀 드리자면, 이건 법률 문제인 것 같습니다. 선을 어떻게 그어야 할까요?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Question / to Speaker, Vethaal_Lovek
#. ALIAS: Dulkehf_Malibor
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMMaliborDulkehf
#. FACE: Question
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Speaker: Doubt does not exist when you are the mouth of the Great Serpent. If I proclaim someone a Zealot, then that is what they are.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109846
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_020_CouncilMeetings_Scene02
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01325D"
msgid "Obviously, if the accused is found guilty, then they deserve the harshest of punishments. If there is any doubt, however..."
msgstr "만약 피의자가 유죄라면 당연히 가장 가혹한 처벌을 받아 마땅합니다. 하지만 의혹이 있는 경우라면..."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Speaker, Kadic_Djimal, Dulkehf_Malibor
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Speaker:  &&& Speaker:  &&& Kadic_Djimal: There is the question of the Zealots, and their continued presence both here and outside of Va'ruun'kai.
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Are you implying, Mediary, that there are Zealot sympathizers among us?
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 0110984B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_020_CouncilMeetings_Scene02
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01325B"
msgid "It's time to take a stance on all who support Jandar's teachings. We must root them out from the inside before the poison spreads."
msgstr "잔다르의 가르침을 지지하는 자들에 대한 입장을 정해야 할 때요. 독이 퍼지기 전에 놈들을 안에서부터 뿌리 뽑아야 하오."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Speaker
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Vethaal_Lovek: And how much time will that take? Not to mention there's no guarantee these people are even capable. &&& Speaker: We will not waste time training the weak. If they are unwilling to serve, they must be culled.
#. ALIAS: Vethaal_Lovek
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMLovekVethaal
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Dulkehf_Malibor: Moving on. Let us proceed to the next item on the agenda.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_PostQuest_CouncilMeetings
#. TOPIC: 01109B4B
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_PostQuest_040_CouncilMeetings_Scene04
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01325A"
msgid "As you command, Speaker."
msgstr "명에 따르겠습니다, 대변자님."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Friendly
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVaericVethaal
#. FACE: Friendly
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVLC04ApostatesRefuge
#. TOPIC: 01109B93
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_LC04_VaericHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "013258"
msgid "I hope you know what this means to me."
msgstr "이게 나한테 무슨 의미인지 너도 알았으면 좋겠어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Worried
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVaericVethaal
#. FACE: Worried
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVLC04ApostatesRefuge
#. TOPIC: 01109B93
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_LC04_VaericHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "013257"
msgid "As much as this may devastate my family, I simply can't go back."
msgstr "이번 일로 우리 가족이 큰 충격을 받겠지만, 그냥 돌아갈 순 없어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Friendly
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVaericVethaal
#. FACE: Friendly
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVLC04ApostatesRefuge
#. TOPIC: 01109B93
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_LC04_VaericHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "013256"
msgid "For the first time, I feel truly free."
msgstr "생전 처음으로 완전히 자유로운 느낌이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Friendly
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVaericVethaal
#. FACE: Friendly
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVLC04ApostatesRefuge
#. TOPIC: 01109B93
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_LC04_VaericHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "013255"
msgid "I know nothing of groat farming, but I hope to learn quickly."
msgstr "그로트 사육에 대해서는 아무것도 모르지만, 빨리 배우고 싶어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Friendly
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVaericVethaal
#. FACE: Friendly
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVLC04ApostatesRefuge
#. TOPIC: 01109B93
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_LC04_VaericHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "013254"
msgid "I am grateful for your understanding."
msgstr "날 이해해 줘서 고마워."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Concerned
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVaericVethaal
#. FACE: Concerned
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVLC04ApostatesRefuge
#. TOPIC: 01109B93
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_LC04_VaericHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "013253"
msgid "I pray my family will move on from my absence soon enough."
msgstr "우리 가족이 내가 없다는 걸 빨리 극복하길 기도하겠어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Grateful
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVaericVethaal
#. FACE: Grateful
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVLC04ApostatesRefuge
#. TOPIC: 01109B93
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_LC04_VaericHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "013252"
msgid "The Mazur's have really helped me stay on my feet."
msgstr "내가 발붙이는 데 매저가 정말 큰 도움을 줬어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Friendly
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVaericVethaal
#. FACE: Friendly
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVLC04ApostatesRefuge
#. TOPIC: 01109B93
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_LC04_VaericHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "013251"
msgid "Groat farming is surprisingly satisfying."
msgstr "그로트 사육이 의외로 만족스럽더라고."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Friendly
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVaericVethaal
#. FACE: Friendly
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVLC04ApostatesRefuge
#. TOPIC: 01109B93
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_LC04_VaericHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "013250"
msgid "I like to think that Vashti is with me. She would've liked this place."
msgstr "바슈티가 나와 함께 있다고 생각하고 싶어. 여동생은 이곳을 좋아했을 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Thinking
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVaericVethaal
#. FACE: Thinking
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVLC04ApostatesRefuge
#. TOPIC: 01109B93
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_LC04_VaericHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "01324F"
msgid "Sometimes I miss the city, but then I remember what being there would mean for me."
msgstr "가끔은 도시가 그립지만, 그럴 때마다 그곳이 나한테 어떤 의미였는지 떠올리지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Thinking
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMVaericVethaal
#. FACE: Thinking
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_DialogueHVLC04ApostatesRefuge
#. TOPIC: 01109B93
#. INFO GROUP: SFBGS001_LC04_VaericHellos
#. TYPE: Miscellaneous
#. SUBTYPE: Hello
msgctxt "01324E"
msgid "The peace and quiet here are a welcome change."
msgstr "이 평화롭고 조용한 분위기가 정말 좋아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Friendly chat / to FemaleCitizen
#. ALIAS: MaleCitizen
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_VaruunGenericMale02
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: FemaleCitizen: The old married couple? Azad and Sherine, if I remember right.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuest
#. TOPIC: 0110A9EB
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuestScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01324D"
msgid "Do you know the scientists out at Hamadi Station?"
msgstr "하마디 기지에 있는 그 과학자들 알아?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to FemaleCitizen
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: MaleCitizen: Do you know the scientists out at Hamadi Station? &&& FemaleCitizen: The old married couple? Azad and Sherine, if I remember right.|I've met them a few times. They seemed a little eccentric, but were otherwise quite nice.
#. ALIAS: MaleCitizen
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_VaruunGenericMale02
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuest
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E9
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuestScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01324C"
msgid "That's them, yes."
msgstr "그 사람들 맞아."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to FemaleCitizen
#. ALIAS: MaleCitizen
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_VaruunGenericMale02
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuest
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E9
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuestScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01324B"
msgid "They're apparently looking for some help with their research."
msgstr "본인들 연구에 도움이 필요한 것처럼 보이더라고."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to FemaleCitizen
#. ALIAS: MaleCitizen
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_VaruunGenericMale02
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: FemaleCitizen: Good luck finding help at a time like this.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuest
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E9
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuestScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "01324A"
msgid "They made some kind of discovery that has them troubled."
msgstr "무슨 발견을 했는데 문제가 있는 모양이야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Azad = uh-ZAHD, Sherine = sheh-REEN / to MaleCitizen
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: MaleCitizen: Do you know the scientists out at Hamadi Station?
#. ALIAS: FemaleCitizen
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_VaruunGenericFemale03
#. FACE: Neutral
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuest
#. TOPIC: 0110A9EA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuestScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013249"
msgid "The old married couple? Azad and Sherine, if I remember right."
msgstr "그 노부부 말이지? 내 기억으로는 아자드랑 셰린일 텐데."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to MaleCitizen
#. ALIAS: FemaleCitizen
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_VaruunGenericFemale03
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: MaleCitizen: That's them, yes.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuest
#. TOPIC: 0110A9EA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuestScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013248"
msgid "I've met them a few times. They seemed a little eccentric, but were otherwise quite nice."
msgstr "몇 번 만나본 적 있어. 좀 별난 구석이 있어 보이긴 해도, 그 외에는 꽤 괜찮던데."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to FemaleCitizen
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: MaleCitizen: That's them, yes.|They're apparently looking for some help with their research.|They made some kind of discovery that has them troubled. &&& FemaleCitizen: Good luck finding help at a time like this.
#. ALIAS: MaleCitizen
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_VaruunGenericMale02
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: FemaleCitizen: Nothing is truly impossible.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuest
#. TOPIC: 0110A9E7
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MS04_TeaserSceneQuestScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "013247"
msgid "Indeed. Yet the Serpent provides for the faithful, so who knows?"
msgstr "그러니까. 그래도 위대한 뱀께서는 신앙인을 도와 주시니, 누가 알겠어?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Doubt / to MaleCitizen
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: FemaleCitizen: The old married couple? Azad and Sherine, if I remember right.|I've met them a few times. They seemed a little eccentric, but were otherwise quite nice. &&& MaleCitizen: That's them, yes.|They're apparently looking for some help with their research.|They made some kind of discovery that has them troubled.
#. ALIAS: FemaleCitizen
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_VaruunGenericFemale03
#. FACE: Neutral
