#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ05_Stage1000_KarijaFinalFG
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0124DA"
msgid "Or you could just let me walk out. We don't have to keep doing this."
msgstr "아니면 날 그냥 보내줘도 되잖아. 이런 짓을 계속 할 필요는 없어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Karija: If you can remove the remaining Interlock, you will have bested us, but you will ruin the lives of those above us.
#. ALIAS: Karija
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFKarijaMaleen
#. FACE: Defiant
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: You're bluffing. Nothing will happen if I shut you down.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ05
#. TOPIC: 010F64B7
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ05_Stage1000_KarijaFinalFG
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0124D9"
msgid "Or we can continue this contest of wills, and see which of us is stronger. The choice is yours."
msgstr "아니면, 이 의지의 시험을 계속할 수도 있어. 누구 의지가 더 강할지 보자고. 선택은 네 몫이다."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Friendly / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Ekris: 
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Friendly
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Ekris: Your lead from House Dul'kehf paid off?
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ05
#. TOPIC: 010F64B0
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ05_Stage1600_EkrisScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0124D8"
msgid "I am old, and my eyesight is not what it used to be, but I know the face of success when I see it."
msgstr "나도 나이 먹어서 눈이 예전 같진 않지만, 성공한 사람 얼굴은 딱 보면 알 수 있지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: You're bluffing. Nothing will happen if I shut you down.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: You're bluffing. Nothing will happen if I shut you down.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFKarijaMaleen
#. FACE: Defiant
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ05
#. TOPIC: 010F64B5
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ05_Stage1000_KarijaFinalFG
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0124D7"
msgid "I have not lied to you from the moment you set foot in here. It is beneath me."
msgstr "네가 여기 발을 들인 순간부터 거짓말은 하지 않았어. 날 뭘로 보는 거냐."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: You're bluffing. Nothing will happen if I shut you down.
#. ALIAS: Player Default
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFKarijaMaleen
#. FACE: Defiant
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ05
#. TOPIC: 010F64B5
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ05_Stage1000_KarijaFinalFG
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0124D6"
msgid "You attempt to stall. I will not abide it."
msgstr "시간을 끌려 하는군. 그런 꼴은 못 보지."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Defiant / to Player Default
#. PROMPT: Or you could just let me walk out. We don't have to keep doing this.
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Player Default: Or you could just let me walk out. We don't have to keep doing this.
#. ALIAS: Karija
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFKarijaMaleen
#. FACE: Defiant
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ05
#. TOPIC: 010F64B1
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ05_Stage1000_KarijaFinalFG
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0124D5"
msgid "But we do. My dedication to the Great Serpent demands my obedience to his Speaker's orders."
msgstr "해야만 한다. 위대한 뱀을 향한 내 헌신이 그분의 대변자가 내린 명령에 복종하길 요구하고 있어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES:  / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Ekris:  &&& Ekris: I am old, and my eyesight is not what it used to be, but I know the face of success when I see it. &&& Ekris: Your lead from House Dul'kehf paid off?
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: PlayerVoiceMale01
#. FACE: Neutral
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: I did not, but it does not surprise me. So many projects over the decades. So many secrets, so few successes.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ05
#. TOPIC: 010F64AC
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ05_Stage1600_EkrisScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0124D4"
msgid "Did you know there was a secret research facility underneath Ma'leen Dam?"
msgstr "마린 댐 아래에 비밀 연구 시설이 있다는 거 알고 있었어요?"

#. SCRIPT NOTES: hero should be dripping with venom / Disgust / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Karija: What is more, you have disrupted the flow of power within the dam. You are one step from dooming those farmers on the surface.
#. ALIAS: Karija
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCFKarijaMaleen
#. FACE: Disgust
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Karija: If you can remove the remaining Interlock, you will have bested us, but you will ruin the lives of those above us.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ05
#. TOPIC: 010F64B9
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ05_Stage1000_KarijaFinalFG
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0124D3"
msgid "All right, hero. You have proven yourself a commendable opponent. But now, you have a choice to make."
msgstr "좋아, 영웅 나리. 넌 스스로가 칭찬받을 만한 적수인 걸 증명했어. 하지만 이제 선택을 해야 할 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Thinking / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Ekris: I have heard of such a thing! Recently, in fact just before the accident. That is apparently not a coincidence.
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Thinking
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ05
#. TOPIC: 010F64AA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ05_Stage1600_EkrisScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0124D2"
msgid "We do not need it for the device, but if this accounts for some of the leaps in progress in the Citadel, you may wish to hold on to it."
msgstr "우리 장치에 필요한 물건은 아니지만, 그게 성채에서 일어나는 현상을 조금이나마 설명해 줄 수 있다면 가지고 있는 게 좋겠어."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Confident / to Player Default
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Confident
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Ekris: Now we await the assistance of Houses Veth'aal and Ka'dic. Let us hope we do not wait long.
#. QUEST: SFBGS001_MQ05
#. TOPIC: 010F64AA
#. SCENE: SFBGS001_MQ05_Stage1600_EkrisScene
#. TYPE: SceneDialogue
#. SUBTYPE: Custom
msgctxt "0124D1"
msgid "As much as I have devoted my life to science, one cannot deny that there is an occasional spark of the Divine. The Great Serpent has use for this, and you, still to come."
msgstr ""
"내가 과학에 평생을 바쳐 왔지만, 가끔은 신적인 불꽃이 튀는 일도 있다는 걸 부정할 순 없으니 말이야. 위대한 뱀께서 이걸 필요로 "
"하신다면, 자네도 곧 필요하게 될 거야."

#. SCRIPT NOTES: Question / to Player Default
#. DIALOGUE BEFORE: Ekris: I am old, and my eyesight is not what it used to be, but I know the face of success when I see it.
#. ALIAS: Ekris
#. VOICE TYPE: SFBGS001_NPCMEkrisKaisir
#. FACE: Question
#. DIALOGUE AFTER: Player Default: [Give Interlock] An old lab produced something called Vortex Interlocks. I have one, and I hope it's helpful.
